      "encoding": "utf8",
      "content": "/* ═══ T.W2-3 · THE OVERTURE GRAMMAR SHEET — the boot subsystem's ONE clock\n * family (t-load-sync §3), colocated with the boot chain (the W1 batch-8\n * colocation law; lifted from App.vue/ColorPicker.vue styles at the W2\n * close PP-8 cap cure — a MOVE, never a removal, feedback_preserve_animations).\n * Every offset below is a token on this shell timeline, so DevTools shows\n * ONE clock. The beats OPEN by gating (useOverture); these rules only voice\n * the staggers/durations. All selectors here are app-unique (verified:\n * `.atmosphere-canvas`, `.pane-shell`, `.hero-blob-anchor` each live in\n * exactly one template), so this global sheet carries the exact semantics\n * the former scoped blocks had. Imported by App.vue after the style.css\n * chain — cascade order preserved. ═══ */\n\n:root {\n    /* B1 · the plate-land family (440ms --spring-snappy; staggers per the\n     * beat sheet: dock +0 · left +40ms · right +120ms). */\n    --overture-plate-land: 440ms;\n    --overture-dock-delay: 0ms;\n    --overture-left-delay: 40ms;\n    --overture-right-delay: 120ms;\n    /* B2 · the field derive-in (0.9s decelerate — t-aurora-boot §2.1). */\n    --overture-derive-in: 0.9s;\n}\n\n/* ── B2 · the atmosphere ARRIVAL (owner ruling 2026-07-05 §1.1, re-cut\n   W2-2 per t-aurora-boot §2.1 step 4): the canvas textures in over its OWN\n   gradient ground once the field is drawable (`isArmed`; immediate on the\n   `\"css\"` placeholder substrate). Ground and field are ONE material by\n   construction (W2-2's ground IS the derived-palette gradient), so the fade\n   cannot pass through gray — the arrival reads as the painting waking up,\n   not a crossfade to a different picture. Duration 0.45s → 0.9s (the §2.1\n   re-cut); decelerate kept, no new curve. W3-2's idle-deferral mechanics\n   untouched (this designs the arrival, it does not revert the deferral). */\n.atmosphere-canvas {\n    opacity: 0;\n    transition: opacity var(--overture-derive-in, 0.9s) var(--ease-decelerate);\n}\n.atmosphere-canvas--arrived {\n    opacity: 1;\n}\n/* PRM-honest (T.W2 gate 5b — the instant-states law): the field is PRESENT\n   at terminal opacity from B0; the arm is a static CONTENT change, never a\n   fade. A bare `transition: none` is NOT enough — the producer's PRM\n   doctrine (glass-ui a11y-overrides.css) FORCES\n   `transition: opacity/color/… 0.1s !important` onto every un-marked\n   element as a state-change fade, so a b2 opacity flip 0→1 still painted a\n   0.1s mid-fade under PRM (annex 2026-07-10: dark leg read 0.5747 — the 5b\n   breach). Pinning opacity to 1 removes the CHANGE, so no forced transition\n   of any duration can fire; pre-arm the canvas buffer is transparent and\n   the same-material gradient ground shows through (one material from t0);\n   a context-loss terminal likewise rests on the ground. */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n    .atmosphere-canvas {\n        opacity: 1;\n        transition: none;\n    }\n}\n\n/* ── B1/B3 · the pane-slot APPEAR grammar (LS-4 — one arrival grammar,\n * three voices): first-mount and late-chunk arrival speak the plate-land\n * family. TRANSFORM ONLY — opacity pinned 1 (the LCP REVEAL-ONLY LAW,\n * PI-2/M-13: the left slot hosts the LCP-owning picker plate; its paint\n * chain never carries an opacity gate). The travel is the plate-land settle\n * (translateY + the cartoon half-degree), NOT the vj-enter off-canvas slide\n * — arrival is a landing, not a swap. */\n.overture-appear-from {\n    transform: translateY(-12px) rotate(-0.6deg);\n}\n.overture-appear-active {\n    transition: transform var(--overture-plate-land) var(--spring-snappy);\n    transition-delay: var(--overture-appear-delay, 0ms);\n}\n.overture-appear-to {\n    transform: none;\n}\n\n/* ── B1 · the dock voice (the M-14 booked-interim): veiled while the\n * producer nub→pill mount-morph runs (the morph is no longer a visible\n * actor), then lands AS the pill through the same family at +0ms. The dock\n * is not the LCP owner, so its land may carry opacity (it was veiled — the\n * reveal IS the arrival). Gating lives in boot/useDockArrival.ts. */\n.overture-dock-veiled {\n    visibility: hidden;\n}\n@keyframes overture-plate-land {\n    from {\n        opacity: 0;\n        transform: translateY(-12px) rotate(-0.6deg);\n    }\n    to {\n        opacity: 1;\n        transform: none;\n    }\n}\n/* ONE-SHOT RELEASE LAW (W2-close finding, live-bisected): every land/emerge\n * beat fills `backwards`, never `both`/`forwards` — each keyframe's `to`\n * state ≡ the element's natural resting state, so releasing at animationend\n * is visually seamless, while a permanently-filling TRANSFORM animation left\n * `current` on the nav rendered every dock control \"element is not stable\"\n * to Playwright actionability FOREVER (20 view-nav specs timed out on real\n * user-shaped clicks — the propose/palette/gradient/walk class). A finished\n * beat retires; it does not squat on the compositor. */\n.overture-dock-land {\n    animation: overture-plate-land var(--overture-plate-land)\n        var(--spring-snappy) var(--overture-dock-delay) backwards;\n}\n\n/* ── B1 · the picker plate's editorial signature (R.W3 Lane E / E1 beat\n * one, RE-CUT at T.W2-3 under THE LCP REVEAL-ONLY LAW, PI-2/M-13): this\n * card IS the page's LCP element (both schemes — the O-24 before-record),\n * so its land is SHADOW ONLY — opacity pinned 1 from B0, transform none\n * (the O-24 breach was exactly this keyframe's former `from { opacity: 0 }`).\n * The MOTION half of the land lives in the slot `appear` grammar above\n * (transform-only); the cartoon shadow CASTS IN as the slot lands — same\n * clock + stagger via the shell tokens. `.pane-shell` is unique to\n * ColorPicker.vue's template, so this global rule binds exactly the plate\n * the former scoped rule did. PRM-gated. */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {\n    @keyframes plate-land {\n        from {\n            box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 transparent;\n        }\n        to {\n            box-shadow: var(--shadow-cartoon);\n        }\n    }\n    .pane-shell > :first-child {\n        /* backwards per the one-shot release law above: the card's natural\n         * box-shadow IS var(--shadow-cartoon) (probed computed-equal), so the\n         * release at animationend is seamless. */\n        animation: plate-land var(--overture-plate-land, 440ms)\n            var(--spring-snappy) var(--overture-appear-delay, 0ms) backwards;\n    }\n}\n\n/* ── B4 · THE EMERGE POSE (T.W2-4, the demo interim; no-pop law): the bead\n * GOO-SCALES from the seat as it mounts at B4 — never a first-frame\n * fully-formed blob. Scale from the seat point (the card-corner anchor),\n * decelerate, ~500ms (the beat sheet's goo-emerge window); the engine's own\n * satellite `emerging` grammar composes inside it. RETIRES to the P6 row-F\n * producer body-arrival pose when it lands (the booked swap).\n * `.hero-blob-anchor` is unique to ColorPicker.vue's template. PRM = static\n * first frame (no animation — the mount IS the state change).\n *\n * T.W4.5 R2 — THE POSE/ARM RACE (lockstep: HeroBlob.vue onEmergeEnd): the\n * engine arms mid-pose and presizes its backing store from gBCR, so the\n * `from { scale(0.35) }` frame poisons the boot resolution to ~0.35× (and\n * a transform never fires the leaf ResizeObserver). HeroBlob releases the\n * race at THIS animation's `animationend` (name-filtered on `blob-emerge`)\n * via the producer's resume re-measure seam. Renaming these keyframes means\n * updating that filter. */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {\n    /* T.W8 · WR-1/T-49a — THE EMERGE RE-CUT TO MATTER-ARRIVAL: the bead\n       goo-SCALES from the seat as MATTER (opaque from frame 1), never fading\n       IN. The α leg is GONE — the no-pop law now holds via SCALE alone (a\n       small droplet growing to full presence, not a translucent ghost\n       resolving). The former `from { opacity: 0 }` compounded with the\n       producer T-60 reveal-bloom's brightness/saturate floor (which stamps AT\n       the fade start and holds through the whole 500ms — t49-research §2.1) to\n       read GRAY on arrival; dropping the α leg removes the demo half of that\n       compound (the bloom half is PRODUCER-ONLY, communiqué §1.1 — an\n       emerge-delay chase is DOA, so NO counter-filter here). The R2 pose/arm\n       race contract is UNCHANGED: the `scale(0.35)` frame + the name filter\n       (`blob-emerge`) HeroBlob.vue's onEmergeEnd keys on both stand — renaming\n       these keyframes still means updating that filter. The wake-gray bead\n       (boot-B, the KeepAlive re-activation flash) is a DISTINCT percept, cured\n       separately in HeroBlob.vue. */\n    @keyframes blob-emerge {\n        from {\n            transform: scale(0.35);\n        }\n        to {\n            transform: none;\n        }\n    }\n    .hero-blob-anchor {\n        /* backwards per the one-shot release law above (`to` ≡ natural). */\n        animation: blob-emerge 500ms var(--ease-decelerate) backwards;\n    }\n}\n\n/* ── PRM — instant states (D3 law 5, kept): the overture collapses; every\n * surface is simply present in its settled pose. (blob-emerge/plate-land\n * above are no-preference-wrapped; the canvas pin is in its own block.) */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n    .overture-appear-from,\n    .overture-appear-to {\n        transform: none;\n    }\n    .overture-appear-active {\n        transition: none;\n    }\n    .overture-dock-land {\n        animation: none;\n    }\n}\n",
