      "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!-- U.W-A11Y · U-F58 (BR-10) — RTL mechanical readiness. `dir=\"ltr\"` is the\n     explicit default-direction plumbing (was absent: `lang` present, `dir` not).\n     The single-locale English tool does NOT do full string extraction (that half\n     is out-of-scope, recorded in the U-F58 decision table); this establishes the\n     `dir` seam so `dir=\"rtl\"` flips the whole document and the grid/flex layout\n     (style.css uses grid + flex + shorthand padding — no global physical\n     left/right positioning) stays integral by construction. Per-component\n     physical-property → logical conversions are BOOKED follow-ups\n     (docs/tranches/U/audit/w-a11y/rtl-logical-property-audit.md). -->\n<html lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">\n    <head>\n        <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n        <meta http-equiv=\"X-UA-Compatible\" content=\"IE=edge\" />\n        <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n        <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Interactive color picker with 15 color spaces, gradient editor, palette browser, and image color extraction. Powered by value.js.\" />\n        <title>Color Picker</title>\n        <link rel=\"icon\" type=\"image/svg+xml\" href=\"./favicon.svg\" />\n\n        <!-- W2-3 (T.W2 · LS-6): Fraunces SELF-HOSTED — the display voice is\n             struck from the network timeline (the Google-Fonts actor RETIRES;\n             zero cross-origin font requests). Variable woff2 (opsz 9..144,\n             wght 100..900), latin + latin-ext, normal + italic, served from\n             ./fonts/. The latin-normal face — the title/hero glyphs — is\n             PRELOADED so it arrives with the critical resources.\n\n             W4-2 (T.W4 · O-10c): the latin-normal face is the tnum-MINTED\n             build (scripts/fonts/build-fraunces-tnum.py — no Fraunces\n             artifact anywhere ships tabular figures; the mint cuts the .tf\n             set the foundry never did: constant-advance composites + a real\n             GSUB tnum feature). The readout's `font-variant-numeric:\n             tabular-nums` is therefore LIVE, verified by rendered\n             digit-advance (never by declaration — the F5 class). -->\n        <!-- (original W2-3 note continues)\n\n             THE BOUNDED INK GATE (D3 [AMENDED-AT-HARDENING M-12]):\n             `font-display: fallback` — a ~100ms UA block period (inside the\n             ≤300ms cap; ink opens on load-or-block-end), then the\n             METRIC-COMPATIBLE fallback below commits; the eventual swap is\n             reflow-free because \"Fraunces Fallback\" is size-adjust-tuned\n             Georgia (measured against the real face: size-adjust 89.26%,\n             ascent 109.79%, descent 29.13%) — never an UNTUNED fallback\n             commit, never a swap-reflow. font-display:fallback's no-late-swap\n             arm is a non-case for a preloaded same-origin face (recorded). -->\n        <link rel=\"preload\" href=\"./fonts/fraunces-latin-normal.woff2\" as=\"font\" type=\"font/woff2\" crossorigin />\n        <style>\n            @font-face {\n                font-family: \"Fraunces\";\n                font-style: normal;\n                font-weight: 100 900;\n                font-display: fallback;\n                src: url(./fonts/fraunces-latin-normal.woff2) format(\"woff2\");\n                unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;\n            }\n            @font-face {\n                font-family: \"Fraunces\";\n                font-style: normal;\n                font-weight: 100 900;\n                font-display: fallback;\n                src: url(./fonts/fraunces-latin-ext-normal.woff2) format(\"woff2\");\n                unicode-range: U+0100-02BA, U+02BD-02C5, U+02C7-02CC, U+02CE-02D7, U+02DD-02FF, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+1D00-1DBF, U+1E00-1E9F, U+1EF2-1EFF, U+2020, U+20A0-20AB, U+20AD-20C0, U+2113, U+2C60-2C7F, U+A720-A7FF;\n            }\n            @font-face {\n                font-family: \"Fraunces\";\n                font-style: italic;\n                font-weight: 100 900;\n                font-display: fallback;\n                src: url(./fonts/fraunces-latin-italic.woff2) format(\"woff2\");\n                unicode-range: U+0000-00FF, U+0131, U+0152-0153, U+02BB-02BC, U+02C6, U+02DA, U+02DC, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+2000-206F, U+20AC, U+2122, U+2191, U+2193, U+2212, U+2215, U+FEFF, U+FFFD;\n            }\n            @font-face {\n                font-family: \"Fraunces\";\n                font-style: italic;\n                font-weight: 100 900;\n                font-display: fallback;\n                src: url(./fonts/fraunces-latin-ext-italic.woff2) format(\"woff2\");\n                unicode-range: U+0100-02BA, U+02BD-02C5, U+02C7-02CC, U+02CE-02D7, U+02DD-02FF, U+0304, U+0308, U+0329, U+1D00-1DBF, U+1E00-1E9F, U+1EF2-1EFF, U+2020, U+20A0-20AB, U+20AD-20C0, U+2113, U+2C60-2C7F, U+A720-A7FF;\n            }\n            /* The metric-compatible fallback (the ink-gate's landing face). */\n            @font-face {\n                font-family: \"Fraunces Fallback\";\n                src: local(\"Georgia\");\n                size-adjust: 89.26%;\n                ascent-override: 109.79%;\n                descent-override: 29.13%;\n                line-gap-override: 0%;\n            }\n        </style>\n\n        <!-- W2-2 (T.W2): the per-stop ground properties, registered PRE-PAINT\n             so the B0 ground can transition. Each is a `<color>` — registered\n             <color> custom properties interpolate in OKLab (CSS Color 4), the\n             chroma-honest path the F-12 ground transition rides. The\n             initial-values are the LIGHT first-visit constants (the boot\n             script below overwrites them — persisted record or the ACTIVE\n             scheme's constant — before first paint; these literals only ever\n             paint if the script itself fails). U-F23: they are SINGLE-SOURCED —\n             the `__GROUND_LIGHT_n__` tokens are injected from boot/ground.ts's\n             FIRST_VISIT_GROUND.light at build/serve time (vite\n             `groundRecordInject` → `injectGroundTokens`), never hand-typed. -->\n        <style>\n            @property --saved-bg-0 { syntax: \"<color>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: __GROUND_LIGHT_0__; }\n            @property --saved-bg-1 { syntax: \"<color>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: __GROUND_LIGHT_1__; }\n            @property --saved-bg-2 { syntax: \"<color>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: __GROUND_LIGHT_2__; }\n            @property --saved-bg-3 { syntax: \"<color>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: __GROUND_LIGHT_3__; }\n            @property --saved-bg   { syntax: \"<color>\"; inherits: true; initial-value: __GROUND_LIGHT_0__; }\n        </style>\n\n        <!-- W2-3 theme-color B0 sub-clause: minted from the persisted ground's\n             base stop by the boot script below, pre-paint; useAtmosphere's\n             sink updates it beside the `--saved-bg` pick transition. The\n             fallback base stop is single-sourced (U-F23 `__GROUND_LIGHT_0__`). -->\n        <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"__GROUND_LIGHT_0__\" />\n\n        <!-- Critical: prevent FOUC before Tailwind CSS loads.\n             Without this, .hidden elements are visible during the\n             CSS/JS race, causing both mobile+desktop panes to render\n             simultaneously, expanding the viewport past 1024px and\n             flipping media queries to desktop mode permanently.\n\n             Uses @layer so that once Tailwind loads, its utilities\n             (lg:flex, lg:block) take priority and override this.\n\n             W2-2: the body ground is the FIXED gradient template over the\n             registered per-stop properties (the same template as style.css's\n             base rule — the producer paletteToCssGradient geometry). The\n             ground is a complete material from the first paint (B0). -->\n        <style>\n            @layer fouc-guard {\n                .hidden { display: none; }\n                body {\n                    background-color: var(--saved-bg);\n                    background-image: linear-gradient(\n                        135deg,\n                        var(--saved-bg-0) 0%,\n                        var(--saved-bg-1) 33%,\n                        var(--saved-bg-2) 67%,\n                        var(--saved-bg-3) 100%\n                    );\n                }\n            }\n        </style>\n\n        <!-- The fouc-guard boot script: scheme FIRST, then the ground.\n             Order is the law (W2-2): resolve the ACTIVE scheme, then paint\n             the persisted gradient ONLY on a scheme+version match — else the\n             ACTIVE scheme's member of the first-visit constant PAIR (dark-\n             honest by construction, F-6: a dark first run never boots as a\n             light-pink page). The persisted shape is `{stops, scheme,\n             deriveVersion}` — STOPS, never a gradient string; the read is\n             shape-validated and falls to the constants on ANY malformation.\n             U-F23 (G-CANON-4): the CONSTANTS (VERSION, the FIRST_VISIT seed,\n             the stop count) are SINGLE-SOURCED — the `__GROUND_*__` tokens are\n             injected from boot/ground.ts at build/serve time (vite\n             `groundRecordInject` → `injectGroundTokens`), so a\n             GROUND_RECORD_VERSION bump propagates here automatically and can no\n             longer strand the boot. Only the guard LOGIC below is mirrored\n             (inherent to a pre-module reader that cannot import). -->\n        <script>\n            (function() {\n                // B0 — the ground beat (the overture's origin mark; O-4 reads it).\n                if (window.performance && performance.mark) performance.mark('overture:b0');\n                var s = document.documentElement.style;\n                // Scheme resolution MIRRORS useColorMode (the producer's own\n                // darkModeSyncScript semantics): the app persists \"auto\" by\n                // default, so \"auto\" MUST honor prefers-dark — the T.W4.5 R1\n                // cure (a returning dark-preference visit used to read \"auto\"\n                // as light and boot the light material, re-theming mid-boot).\n                var stored = localStorage.getItem('vueuse-color-scheme');\n                var prefersDark = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;\n                var dark = stored === 'dark' || ((stored === 'auto' || !stored) && prefersDark);\n                if (dark) document.documentElement.classList.add('dark');\n                s.colorScheme = dark ? 'dark' : 'light';\n\n                // The first-visit constant PAIR + the version + the stop count\n                // are SINGLE-SOURCED from boot/ground.ts (U-F23): the\n                // `__GROUND_*__` tokens are injected by vite's\n                // `injectGroundTokens` at build/serve time, so a\n                // GROUND_RECORD_VERSION bump propagates here and never strands\n                // the boot. (dark = the producer derive's dark band — honest\n                // for a dark first run.)\n                var FIRST_VISIT = __GROUND_FIRST_VISIT__;\n                var VERSION = __GROUND_RECORD_VERSION__;\n                var scheme = dark ? 'dark' : 'light';\n                var stops = FIRST_VISIT[scheme];\n                try {\n                    var rec = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('color-picker-ground'));\n                    if (rec && rec.deriveVersion === VERSION &&\n                        rec.scheme === scheme &&\n                        Array.isArray(rec.stops) && rec.stops.length === __GROUND_STOP_COUNT__ &&\n                        rec.stops.every(function (x) { return /^#[0-9a-fA-F]{6}$/.test(String(x)); })) {\n                        stops = rec.stops;\n                    }\n                } catch (e) { /* malformed record → the constants */ }\n                for (var i = 0; i < __GROUND_STOP_COUNT__; i++) {\n                    s.setProperty('--saved-bg-' + i, stops[i]);\n                }\n                s.setProperty('--saved-bg', stops[0]);\n                // theme-color rides the ground's base stop from B0.\n                var meta = document.querySelector('meta[name=\"theme-color\"]');\n                if (meta) meta.setAttribute('content', stops[0]);\n            })();\n        </script>\n\n        <script type=\"module\" src=\"./main.ts\"></script>\n    </head>\n\n    <!-- W6-8 (S.W6 · card-lighting forensics artifact 1): the body IS the\n         atmosphere/field plane host — it paints the `--saved-bg` derived\n         ground and contains the aurora canvas AND every teleported overlay.\n         `data-paper-field` is glass-ui's field contract: under this ancestor,\n         the producer's orphan-card warm field-floor fallback (cards.css\n         presence-behind gate) switches OFF, so every glass card — portaled\n         dialogs included — reads the REAL atmosphere through the glass instead\n         of painting its own interior amber lamp. One attribute; no local glass\n         recipe. -->\n    <body class=\"relative\" id=\"app\" data-paper-field></body>\n</html>\n",
