        "content": "/* U-F9 — THE PICKER HEADER GRAMMAR: the one-law rhythm (Row A · T-2/T-51/T-59)\n * + the whole-header scroll contraction (Row B · T-61/§0.8 owner-verbatim).\n *\n * Colocated global sheet (the seat.css / overture.css precedent — imported by\n * ColorPicker.vue's <script setup>). Two reasons it is GLOBAL, not scoped:\n *   1. every selector is UNIQUE to ColorPicker's template (`.picker-header`,\n *      `.header-sentinel`), so a global rule binds identically to a scoped one\n *      (the PP-8 cap-seam precedent);\n *   2. the contraction re-keys the light-DOM CHILD-component classes\n *      (`.space-trigger` in ColorSpaceSelector, `.readout` in\n *      ColorComponentDisplay) — a global (un-hashed) sheet reaches them through\n *      the PLAIN descendant selector, the exact form glass-ui's own\n *      `card-scroll.css` uses to reach `[data-slot=card-title]` (no `:deep()`\n *      scope-escape needed, and no `:deep()` into shadcn internals — these are\n *      the demo's own custom classes on custom components).\n */\n\n/* ── Row A · ONE rhythm law ──────────────────────────────────────────────\n * The title→readout seam is governed by ONE container-scaled token at every\n * viewport, replacing the fixed `gap-y-1` (4px) that — over the fp-derived\n * blob-reservation band — read as a 6× divergent gap (4.0px@1440 vs\n * 24.6px@390). The token is `cqi`-scaled (the pane-slot container), so 1440\n * and 390 share ONE rhythm SOURCE (the `<lg` band switch is dead). */\n.picker-header {\n    --picker-header-rhythm: clamp(0.25rem, 1.4cqi, 0.55rem);\n    row-gap: var(--picker-header-rhythm);\n    position: sticky;\n    top: 0;\n    /* the whole block condenses as ONE strip — a SINGLE discrete transition on\n     * the threshold crossing (never a per-scroll-frame scrub): the padding\n     * band + the type rung + the veil move together. Bounded 300ms reflow at\n     * the crossing, ZERO per-frame reflow during scroll (the honest box shrink\n     * §0.8 demands, without the CLS the producer's compositor gate guards). */\n    transition:\n        padding-top var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-standard),\n        padding-bottom var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-standard);\n}\n\n/* the 0-height scroll sentinel rides the top of the Card scroll container;\n * useHeaderCondense observes it, flipping `.is-condensed` past the threshold. */\n.header-sentinel {\n    height: 0;\n    margin: 0;\n    padding: 0;\n    pointer-events: none;\n}\n\n/* ── Row B · THE BACKGROUND BAND (§0.8 \"background band\") ─────────────────\n * The strip's veil: the plate's rung-1 material (`--glass-bg-resting` +\n * `--glass-blur-resting`, the PaneHeader idiom — DESIGN §Surfaces \"the veil is\n * the plate's own rung-1 material at a scroll-earned intensity\") at 0 opacity\n * AT REST (the header stays transparent-on-plate — T-23 at-rest STANDS) and\n * FULL when condensed, so the scrolled Components rows never ghost-through the\n * strip (t33-research §6.6 — the pinned defect). Feathered 12px past the box\n * so the band dissolves into the plate, never terminating at a hard edge. */\n.picker-header::before {\n    content: \"\";\n    position: absolute;\n    inset: 0 0 -12px 0;\n    z-index: -1;\n    pointer-events: none;\n    background: var(--glass-bg-resting);\n    -webkit-backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur-resting);\n    backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur-resting);\n    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(\n        to bottom,\n        black calc(100% - 12px),\n        transparent\n    );\n    mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, black calc(100% - 12px), transparent);\n    border-radius: inherit;\n    opacity: 0;\n    transition: opacity var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-standard);\n}\n.picker-header.is-condensed::before {\n    opacity: 1;\n}\n\n/* ── Row B · THE PADDING CONTRACTION (§0.8 \"padding\") ─────────────────────\n * The band's vertical padding contracts on condense (a REAL layout-box shrink,\n * measurable by getComputedStyle — BR-9; NOT a compositor translate). */\n.picker-header.is-condensed {\n    padding-top: 0.375rem;\n    padding-bottom: 0.375rem;\n}\n\n/* ── Row B · THE TITLE STEP (§0.8 \"title\" · BR-11) ───────────────────────\n * The title steps ONE real golden rung down on condense — `--type-display-2`\n * (at-rest, BR-4 must-STAY, untouched) → `--type-display-1`. A REAL TOKEN STEP,\n * never a compositor `scale()` of the un-stepped rung. `--type-display-1`\n * floors at 1.618rem (25.9px @390 / 41.9px @1440) — above the legibility floor\n * the wave doc names (BR-11: the T-42 \"text too small\" below-bound). The\n * `.space-trigger`'s own font-size transition rides here so the step is smooth,\n * not a jump. */\n.picker-header .space-trigger {\n    transition:\n        color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-standard),\n        font-size var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-standard);\n}\n.picker-header.is-condensed .space-trigger {\n    font-size: var(--type-display-1);\n}\n\n/* the readout condenses to a compact single-line register — the value stays\n * legible while scrolled (the picker's data never leaves the strip), and the\n * 2-line lock's reserved air collapses so the strip is SHORT (the block-size\n * contraction that makes BR-9 measurable at the readout too). Card-lock in the\n * scrolled state is moot — a scroll gesture is not a value change. */\n/* the readout SNAPS on condense (no transition on its font-size or line-lock\n * min-height): that reservation IS the card-lock — it re-sizes only on a SPACE\n * change (--readout-lines / --readout-fit), and the O-10b line-lock census\n * measures both discretely — so animating them would both violate the lock and\n * be caught mid-transition. The dominant contraction feel rides the title +\n * padding + veil transitions; the compact readout resolves in one step under\n * them. */\n.picker-header.is-condensed .readout {\n    font-size: var(--type-display-1);\n    min-height: 1.12em;\n    align-content: start;\n}\n\n/* the strip is TIGHT: the blob's at-rest vertical reservation on the title row\n * (seat.css `--blob-fp`-derived min-height, which seats the at-rest readout\n * BELOW the bead) is released on condense — the condensed readout is the\n * narrower display-1 rung, so it clears the corner bead HORIZONTALLY (left\n * column) and can sit flush under the title. This is what makes the strip read\n * as ONE short band, not a tall header with a smaller title. */\n.picker-header.is-condensed .title-row {\n    min-height: 0;\n}\n\n/* Reduced motion: the condense STATE still lands (it is a designed layout\n * state, not decorative motion), but the transitions collapse to instant under\n * the global PRM guard (animations.css) — the box shrinks without the 300ms\n * scrub, exactly as a discrete state should. */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n    .picker-header,\n    .picker-header .space-trigger,\n    .picker-header .readout,\n    .picker-header::before {\n        transition-duration: 0.01ms;\n    }\n}\n"
      },
