      "content": "/* Project-specific keyframe animations.\n * Shared keyframes (dialog, floating-panel, card-menu, shimmer, etc.)\n * are provided by @mkbabb/glass-ui/styles/animations.css. */\n\n/* --- Edit drawer entrance (value.js-specific) --- */\n\n@keyframes edit-drawer-in {\n    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateX(-100%) translateY(-50%); }\n    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateX(0) translateY(-50%); }\n}\n\n/* INTENTIONAL media-query keyframe override: on mobile (≤ 639 px) the drawer\n * is centred rather than slide-in from the left, so the geometry differs\n * entirely. A media-query @keyframes redefinition is legal CSS (the UA picks\n * the whole matching block); the mobile variant intentionally restates all\n * frames so nothing is inherited from the desktop block. */\n@media (max-width: 639px) {\n    @keyframes edit-drawer-in {\n        from { opacity: 0; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(0.85); }\n        to   { opacity: 1; transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(1); }\n    }\n}\n\n/* --- Staggered-children entrance (N.W5.E) -----------------------------------\n * The intended affordance behind the `.stagger-children` class on\n * ComponentSliders' channel grid (defined-or-removed at N.W5.E; kept — the\n * `animationKey` :key remount machinery exists expressly to re-fire it on\n * color-space change). Each direct child fades + rises in, offset by index, so\n * the slider rows cascade rather than pop. The entrance is one-shot.\n *\n * inv-N-9 PRM: the whole utility lives inside `no-preference`, so under\n * reduced-motion the children simply render in place with no transform/opacity\n * keyframe at all (belt-and-suspenders with the global reduce-guard below). */\n@keyframes stagger-child-in {\n    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(0.5rem); }\n    to   { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); }\n}\n\n/* R.W3 Lane E / E1: `--stagger-base` lets an orchestrator push the whole\n * cascade later in a timeline (the picker's plate-land → field paint-in →\n * channel stagger three-beat sets it for the opening breath only); unset it\n * resolves to 0ms and the utility behaves exactly as before. */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {\n    .stagger-children > * {\n        animation: stagger-child-in var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-standard) both;\n    }\n    .stagger-children > *:nth-child(1) { animation-delay: calc(var(--stagger-base, 0ms) + 0ms); }\n    .stagger-children > *:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: calc(var(--stagger-base, 0ms) + 40ms); }\n    .stagger-children > *:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: calc(var(--stagger-base, 0ms) + 80ms); }\n    .stagger-children > *:nth-child(4) { animation-delay: calc(var(--stagger-base, 0ms) + 120ms); }\n    .stagger-children > *:nth-child(5) { animation-delay: calc(var(--stagger-base, 0ms) + 160ms); }\n    .stagger-children > *:nth-child(6) { animation-delay: calc(var(--stagger-base, 0ms) + 200ms); }\n    .stagger-children > *:nth-child(n + 7) { animation-delay: calc(var(--stagger-base, 0ms) + 240ms); }\n}\n\n/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n * THE THREE MOTION FAMILIES (R.W4 Lane B / B1 — U12)\n *\n * Every Vue <Transition>/<TransitionGroup> in the demo keys exactly ONE of\n * three named families; a fourth name is a defect (gate (a), R.W4 §Hard\n * gate). The family owns the CURVE + TOKEN pairing; a consuming site may\n * parameterise only GEOMETRY through the `--vj-*` custom properties (set on\n * the transitioning element or an ancestor — custom props inherit). The\n * standing inventory + per-site mapping lives at\n * docs/tranches/R/audit/R.W4-visual-runtime/transition-inventory.md.\n *\n *   vj-enter     — a surface ARRIVES or DEPARTS (panes, overlays, drawers,\n *                  toolbars, list items). Spring-smooth entrance, accelerate\n *                  exit. Geometry: --vj-enter-x/-y/-rot/-scale/-opacity.\n *   vj-morph     — ONE surface, NEW content (in-place swaps: results, icon\n *                  cycles, slug bar, rename reveal). Snappy spring, fast\n *                  fades; optional height morph via --vj-morph-collapse/\n *                  -expanded. Geometry: --vj-morph-x/-y/-scale (+ mirrored\n *                  exit via --vj-morph-exit-x/-y).\n *   vj-celebrate — a ONE-SHOT feedback beat (saved!, error pop). Bouncy\n *                  spring entrance, quick retire. Geometry:\n *                  --vj-celebrate-x/-y/-scale (+ collapse/expanded).\n *\n * The global prefers-reduced-motion guard below neutralises all three.\n * ----------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n\n/* ── Family 1 · enter/exit ── */\n.vj-enter-enter-active {\n    transition:\n        opacity var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-decelerate),\n        transform var(--spring-smooth-duration) var(--spring-smooth);\n}\n.vj-enter-leave-active {\n    transition:\n        opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-accelerate),\n        transform var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-accelerate);\n}\n.vj-enter-enter-from,\n.vj-enter-leave-to {\n    opacity: var(--vj-enter-opacity, 0);\n    transform: translate(var(--vj-enter-x, 0px), var(--vj-enter-y, 0.5rem))\n        rotate(var(--vj-enter-rot, 0deg)) scale(var(--vj-enter-scale, 1));\n}\n.vj-enter-move {\n    transition: transform var(--spring-smooth-duration) var(--spring-smooth);\n}\n\n/* ── Family 2 · morph ── */\n.vj-morph-enter-active {\n    transition:\n        opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-decelerate),\n        transform var(--spring-snappy-duration) var(--spring-snappy),\n        max-height var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-decelerate);\n    overflow: hidden;\n}\n.vj-morph-leave-active {\n    transition:\n        opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-accelerate),\n        transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-accelerate),\n        max-height var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-accelerate);\n    overflow: hidden;\n}\n.vj-morph-enter-from {\n    opacity: 0;\n    transform: translate(var(--vj-morph-x, 0px), var(--vj-morph-y, 0.25rem))\n        scale(var(--vj-morph-scale, 0.97));\n    max-height: var(--vj-morph-collapse, none);\n}\n.vj-morph-leave-to {\n    opacity: 0;\n    transform: translate(\n            var(--vj-morph-exit-x, calc(-1 * var(--vj-morph-x, 0px))),\n            var(--vj-morph-exit-y, calc(-1 * var(--vj-morph-y, 0.25rem)))\n        )\n        scale(var(--vj-morph-scale, 0.97));\n    max-height: var(--vj-morph-collapse, none);\n}\n.vj-morph-enter-to,\n.vj-morph-leave-from {\n    max-height: var(--vj-morph-expanded, none);\n}\n.vj-morph-move {\n    transition: transform var(--spring-snappy-duration) var(--spring-snappy);\n}\n\n/* ── Family 3 · celebration ── */\n.vj-celebrate-enter-active {\n    transition:\n        opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-decelerate),\n        transform var(--spring-bouncy-duration) var(--spring-bouncy),\n        max-height var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-decelerate);\n    overflow: hidden;\n}\n.vj-celebrate-leave-active {\n    transition:\n        opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-accelerate),\n        transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-accelerate),\n        max-height var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-accelerate);\n    overflow: hidden;\n}\n.vj-celebrate-enter-from,\n.vj-celebrate-leave-to {\n    opacity: 0;\n    transform: translate(var(--vj-celebrate-x, 0px), var(--vj-celebrate-y, 0px))\n        scale(var(--vj-celebrate-scale, 0.9));\n    max-height: var(--vj-celebrate-collapse, none);\n}\n.vj-celebrate-enter-to,\n.vj-celebrate-leave-from {\n    max-height: var(--vj-celebrate-expanded, none);\n}\n\n/* The view-select settle beat (B3) — the dock body confirms a view switch\n * with a one-shot morph-family settle (snappy spring, scale only). */\n@keyframes vj-settle {\n    0% { transform: scale(1); }\n    35% { transform: scale(1.03); }\n    100% { transform: scale(1); }\n}\n\n/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n * Global prefers-reduced-motion guard\n * Neutralises CSS keyframe animations and transitions app-wide for users\n * who have requested reduced motion in their OS/browser settings.\n * The goo-blob WebGL RAF loop is handled separately in useMetaballRenderer\n * (single-frame render on reduced-motion).  The aurora RAF is glass-ui-owned\n * and honours the query internally.\n * ----------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n    *,\n    *::before,\n    *::after {\n        animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;\n        animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;\n        transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;\n        scroll-behavior: auto !important;\n    }\n}\n\n/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n * Reduced-motion overlay opacity carve-out (B.W1 Lane B)\n * The global guard above is too blunt for reka-ui Dialog/Sheet/Popover\n * overlays, which drive transitions off [data-state]. This block MUST\n * come after the global guard so its later source order wins the cascade\n * over `transition-duration: 0.01ms` (equal specificity, equal !important).\n * ----------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n    /* keep state-change opacity fades on overlay primitives — the fade\n     * communicates state without inducing vestibular stress. */\n    [data-state=\"open\"],\n    [data-state=\"closed\"],\n    [data-state=\"open\"]::before,\n    [data-state=\"closed\"]::after {\n        transition-duration: 150ms !important;\n        transition-property: opacity !important;\n    }\n}\n\n/* -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n * Pane swap — the App-shell enter/exit family (R.W4 Lane B / B1; moved\n * here from App.vue's unscoped block at the T.W2-close PP-8 cap cure —\n * it overrides the vj-enter base family THIS file hosts, so this is its\n * cohesion home. Higher-specificity direct-child overrides: source order\n * vs the base family is immaterial.)\n * The former pane-slide/pane-left/pane-right trio collapsed onto\n * `vj-enter`; these DIRECT-CHILD geometry overrides carry only the pane\n * slots' off-canvas slide + cartoon-swagger rotate, opacity pinned (the\n * swap reads as travel, not a fade). Direct-child (`>`) on purpose: an\n * inherited `--vj-enter-*` var would leak the pane geometry into nested\n * in-pane transitions. The PaneSlot <Transition> stays DEFAULT mode (the\n * R.W3 dev-safe simultaneous cross-slide — DESIGN.md §Motion).\n * ----------------------------------------------------------------------- */\n.pane-wrapper--left > .vj-enter-enter-from,\n.pane-wrapper--left > .vj-enter-leave-to {\n    opacity: 1;\n    transform: translateX(-110%) rotate(-2deg);\n}\n.pane-wrapper--right > .vj-enter-enter-from,\n.pane-wrapper--right > .vj-enter-leave-to {\n    opacity: 1;\n    transform: translateX(110%) rotate(2deg);\n}\n\n/* W3-4 (S.W3): promote the pane to its own compositor layer for the\n * DURATION of the enter/leave transition ONLY (`*-active`) — never a\n * standing `will-change` layer. The browser drops the hint the moment the\n * transition class is removed. */\n.pane-wrapper--left > .vj-enter-enter-active,\n.pane-wrapper--left > .vj-enter-leave-active,\n.pane-wrapper--right > .vj-enter-enter-active,\n.pane-wrapper--right > .vj-enter-leave-active {\n    will-change: transform;\n}\n\n/* T.W5 · R2+R3 (T-14 / D7 — the two-channel law; one moment, one clock):\n * the pane swap is a SPATIAL travel, so the ENTER rides `--spring-snappy`\n * at the spring's OWN clock. The superseded W3-5 retune kept the smooth\n * curve but squeezed it onto `--duration-normal` — the named\n * normalized-spring-on-generic-clock anti-pattern (a spring linear()\n * reaches ~0.5 by ~6% of ANY clock → all travel in the first ~60ms,\n * then dead air; t-transitions-liquid F2). PKT-2 (the ~0.3s preset) is\n * unanswered at this cut, so the swap lands on arm (i) —\n * `--spring-snappy` @ `--spring-snappy-duration` (0.4s true settle);\n * decision recorded on the T.md §7.2 book row.\n * The LEAVE is the exit law: strictly SHORTER than the enter, bezier\n * `--ease-out`, never an overshoot — the outgoing plate is gone before\n * the incoming plate's overshoot lands (the prior full-0.3s ACCELERATE\n * leave held the outgoing pane at full presence exactly when the\n * incoming pane arrived — the F2 mid-flight collision). Both rules stay\n * SCOPED to the pane wrappers: the un-scoped vj-enter family above is\n * the F6 KEEP set, untouched. */\n.pane-wrapper--left > .vj-enter-enter-active,\n.pane-wrapper--right > .vj-enter-enter-active {\n    transition:\n        opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-decelerate),\n        transform var(--spring-snappy-duration) var(--spring-snappy);\n}\n.pane-wrapper--left > .vj-enter-leave-active,\n.pane-wrapper--right > .vj-enter-leave-active {\n    transition:\n        opacity var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out),\n        transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-out);\n}\n",
