      "sha256": "cf8af954242f78b2048073b729c37ad2532776a3bf19bfce17f4f84d90640535",
      "encoding": "utf8",
      "content": "/*\n * ── The dual-contrast focus-ring recipe (U.W-A11Y · U-F25) ──────────────────\n *\n * ONE token recipe reused by every keyboard-operable control (the gradient\n * stop handles + remove chip today; the modality lane REFERENCES these names\n * from style.css for its forced-colors/prefers-contrast register — never a\n * per-control literal).\n *\n * The U-F25 defect had TWO deaths: (1) an inline `boxShadow` on the control\n * CLOBBERED Tailwind's `focus-visible:ring-2` box-shadow layer, and (2) the\n * `--ring`/`--color-ring` token it reached resolved EMPTY — so even an\n * un-clobbered ring painted nothing. This recipe cures (2): both channels\n * resolve to REAL, non-empty colors by construction. The cascade half of the\n * cure — hoisting the material shadow off the inline style so the ring\n * COMPOSES with it — lives in the control's own scoped CSS (Pole A).\n *\n * The affordance is DUAL-CONTRAST — a 1px inner DARK hairline riding UNDER a\n * 3px outer LIGHT ring — so at least one edge contrasts against ANY fill the\n * ring rides over (a gradient stop's own colour, a slider thumb, a swatch).\n * The two neutral poles are the ROBUST default (they read on every hue); the\n * branded alternative — binding the outer ring to the WCAG-guarded\n * `--accent-view` (post-U-F26) — is the bracket's other pole, left as a\n * one-line retune for the owner. Scheme-independent by design: the ring rides\n * over the control's own fill, not the page, so it must read the same in light\n * and dark.\n *\n * Composed by every control as:\n *   box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--focus-ring-inner),\n *               0 0 0 3px var(--focus-ring-outer),\n *               var(--shadow-sm);\n * with a forced-colors `outline` fallback (box-shadow is stripped in WHCM).\n */\n:root {\n    --focus-ring-inner: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85);\n    --focus-ring-outer: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);\n}\n",
      "live": {
        "absent": false,
        "bytes": 1911,
        "mode": "0644",
        "nlink": 1,
        "sha256": "cf8af954242f78b2048073b729c37ad2532776a3bf19bfce17f4f84d90640535",
        "content": "/*\n * ── The dual-contrast focus-ring recipe (U.W-A11Y · U-F25) ──────────────────\n *\n * ONE token recipe reused by every keyboard-operable control (the gradient\n * stop handles + remove chip today; the modality lane REFERENCES these names\n * from style.css for its forced-colors/prefers-contrast register — never a\n * per-control literal).\n *\n * The U-F25 defect had TWO deaths: (1) an inline `boxShadow` on the control\n * CLOBBERED Tailwind's `focus-visible:ring-2` box-shadow layer, and (2) the\n * `--ring`/`--color-ring` token it reached resolved EMPTY — so even an\n * un-clobbered ring painted nothing. This recipe cures (2): both channels\n * resolve to REAL, non-empty colors by construction. The cascade half of the\n * cure — hoisting the material shadow off the inline style so the ring\n * COMPOSES with it — lives in the control's own scoped CSS (Pole A).\n *\n * The affordance is DUAL-CONTRAST — a 1px inner DARK hairline riding UNDER a\n * 3px outer LIGHT ring — so at least one edge contrasts against ANY fill the\n * ring rides over (a gradient stop's own colour, a slider thumb, a swatch).\n * The two neutral poles are the ROBUST default (they read on every hue); the\n * branded alternative — binding the outer ring to the WCAG-guarded\n * `--accent-view` (post-U-F26) — is the bracket's other pole, left as a\n * one-line retune for the owner. Scheme-independent by design: the ring rides\n * over the control's own fill, not the page, so it must read the same in light\n * and dark.\n *\n * Composed by every control as:\n *   box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px var(--focus-ring-inner),\n *               0 0 0 3px var(--focus-ring-outer),\n *               var(--shadow-sm);\n * with a forced-colors `outline` fallback (box-shadow is stripped in WHCM).\n */\n:root {\n    --focus-ring-inner: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85);\n    --focus-ring-outer: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);\n}\n"
      },
