      "encoding": "utf8",
      "content": "@import \"tailwindcss\";\n@import \"tw-animate-css\";\n\n/*\n * EXPLICIT demo-source scan (N.W2.B — the desktop-pane-visibility P0 fix).\n *\n * The desktop dual-pane vs. mobile single-slot layout toggles on the\n * `[data-layout]` stamp App.vue sets on `.app-layout` from the single\n * `isDesktop` truth (MOB-1, T round-4 — the display witnesses live in this file,\n * below; the retired width-only `lg:*` utilities no longer gate pane\n * visibility). The one surviving JIT-scanned utility on the pane wrappers is\n * the mobile slot's `sm:max-w-lg` width clamp: with it unemitted the mobile\n * plate loses its ≥40rem clamp (K.W2.6 §2, audit/lanes/C9.md §1.1). The scan\n * still covers the FULL demo utility surface (every `lg:*`/`sm:*`/… the tree\n * uses), so the explicit `@source` below stays load-bearing regardless.\n *\n * Tailwind v4 auto-detection roots its scan at the GIT REPOSITORY ROOT and\n * prunes `.gitignore` matches; that *happens* to cover App.vue today, but the\n * coverage is implicit — it silently evaporates outside a git checkout, or if\n * `demo/` is ever gitignored, exactly the P9 phantom-utility failure mode\n * (inv-N-7). The two `@source` directives below (declared after the glass-ui\n * `@import`s) make the demo-author tree's scan EXPLICIT and git-independent.\n * The paths resolve relative to THIS file (`demo/@/styles/`): `../../color-picker`\n * reaches the App.vue shell, `..` reaches the `@/` component/composable tree.\n * Scoped to the authored CODE files by extension (`{vue,ts,html}`) so the\n * sibling `.css` files (this one + animations.css/utils.css) — which are NOT\n * content templates — stay out of the candidate-extraction set.\n *\n * The CI emission probe (.github/workflows/ci.yml → scripts/ci/css-emission-probe.mjs)\n * asserts the pane-visibility witnesses survive the build — the `[data-layout]`\n * display rules (present, un-media'd) + the `sm:max-w-lg` clamp (gated at 40rem)\n * — so a future scan/emission regression fails loud instead of shipping a blank\n * desktop.\n */\n\n/*\n * Glass-ui imports the two orthogonal distribution surfaces glass-ui ships\n * (post-9275584 — E.W0 Lane A adoption, closes contract-v2 §2.1 keystone gap):\n *\n *   `./styles`     — Tailwind-source surface (src/styles/index.css):\n *                    tokens.css, typography.css (@font-face + url(\"../fonts/…\")),\n *                    theme.css (@theme aliases), glass/paper/dock/cards/...\n *                    utilities, and `@source \"../components\"` for Tailwind's\n *                    class-scanning over glass-ui's component tree. This path\n *                    MUST be processed by the consumer's Tailwind compiler\n *                    (its semantics depend on Tailwind v4 `@theme` + `@source`).\n *\n *   `./styles.css` — Compiled SFC-scoped surface (dist/glass-ui.css):\n *                    Vue <style scoped> output (data-v-* attribute selectors)\n *                    for glass-ui's components. Pre-compiled; consumed as-is.\n *\n * The two are complementary, not substitutes: the Tailwind-source path carries\n * design-system tokens + font-face + utilities; the compiled path carries\n * SFC-scoped component CSS. Both are needed for a faithful glass-ui render.\n */\n@import \"@mkbabb/glass-ui/styles\";\n@import \"@mkbabb/glass-ui/styles.css\";\n/* The brand font corpus (R.W3 Lane A / A1 — U1-fonts): real Plus Jakarta Sans +\n * Fira Code woff2 faces (base64, variable-weight). Deliberately split off the\n * critical `./styles` path by the producer; the metric-compat *Fallback* faces\n * (ascent-override/size-adjust) ship in that critical `./styles` surface, so the\n * body/mono voices paint correct-METRIC glyphs at first paint even before the\n * real faces arrive — zero layout shift when they swap in.\n *\n * S.W3-9 (CSS critical-path diet): the corpus is base64 woff2 worth ~102 KB gzip\n * — the ENTIRE render-blocking overage over the ≤120 KB gate (everything else\n * render-blocking is ~86 KB gzip, already under). It is therefore DEFERRED off\n * the critical `<link>`: the `deferGlassFonts` vite plugin (plugins/vite-defer-\n * glass-fonts.ts) replaces the marker below with the real `@import` in DEV (dev\n * is not gate-measured; render-blocking there is faithful) and, in the BUILD,\n * emits the corpus as a standalone hashed asset loaded via a non-blocking\n * `<link media=print onload=…>` (the same idiom index.html uses for Fraunces).\n * The critical/deferred split of glass-ui's `./styles` MONOLITH itself is a\n * producer concern — see the census artefact's producer-letter record. */\n/*__GLASS_FONTS_DEFERRED__*/\n@import \"./animations.css\";\n/* The house code-plate ink (S.W4-8): ONE hljs token theme — crayon primaries\n * proportioned, Fira, dark via `.dark` — consumed by the docs' build-time\n * TypeScript plates AND the gradient pane's live CSS editor. The former\n * GitHub-css imports + per-component head-injection swaps are dead. */\n@import \"./hljs.css\";\n/* The app-shell LAYOUT surface (W43 · RF-15 §b 5): the dock-atop band grid,\n * pane container/wrappers, [data-layout] witnesses + the T-45 pane-card blur\n * seat, split out of this file. It consumes foundation's layout tokens. */\n@import \"./shell.css\";\n\n/* The explicit demo-source scan (see the header block) — declared AFTER the\n * glass-ui `@import`s so its `@utility` registrations (text-mono-small &c.,\n * consumed by `.slug-pill`'s `@apply` below) are in scope before any candidate\n * extraction runs. */\n@source \"../../color-picker/**/*.{vue,ts,html}\";\n@source \"../**/*.{vue,ts,html}\";\n\n@theme {\n    /* The dead `--font-display`/`--font-serif`/`--font-mono` re-declarations are\n     * DELETED (R.W3 Lane A / A1): re-pinning the Tailwind theme keys only moved\n     * the runtime var, never what glass-ui's own compiled display rungs paint —\n     * the `@theme inline` split-brain. The display voice is now cured at the\n     * SOURCE token (`--font-stack-display`, `:root` below); the mono/serif keys\n     * resolve through glass-ui's bridges (`--font-mono` → --font-stack-mono →\n     * Fira Code; `--font-serif` → --font-stack-text → Jakarta, the body voice —\n     * the three-voice law reserves Fraunces for display rungs only). */\n\n    --color-gold: #D4AF37;\n    --color-gold-light: #F5E6A3;\n\n    /* ── Demo-local layout token bridges (D.W4 Lane A) ──\n     * Surface the demo's :root layout tokens as Tailwind utility keys so\n     * consumers write `min-w-menu` instead of `min-w-[var(--menu-min-w)]` etc.\n     * Glass-ui already bridges --z-index-*, --transition-duration-*, --radius-*,\n     * --shadow-card, --ease-* (see node_modules/@mkbabb/glass-ui … theme.css).\n     * (The `max-w-desktop-pane` bridge died with the self-clamp fork at R.W3\n     * Lane A — the grid owns the clamp; see the pane clamp ladder in :root.\n     * The `top-dock-inset` bridge died with the fixed dock overlay at T.W6 ·\n     * T-31 — the dock band is in-flow grid structure now; --dock-inset is the\n     * shell's own top padding.) */\n    --max-width-tooltip:      12.5rem;\n    --min-width-menu:         var(--menu-min-w);\n    --shadow-card-hover:      var(--shadow-cartoon-hover);\n\n    /* ── The bare-utility transition default (S.W3-5) ──\n     * Tailwind v4's un-modified `transition` / `transition-*` utilities fall\n     * back to a hard-coded 150ms `cubic-bezier(0.4,0,0.2,1)`. The 21-file\n     * bare-utility census (motion-animation-inventory §5) inherits that\n     * untokened default. Alias it at the `@theme` ROOT to the house motion\n     * tokens so every un-tuned `transition` utility speaks the app's fast\n     * duration + standard ease by construction — no per-callsite modifier. */\n    --default-transition-duration:         var(--duration-fast);\n    --default-transition-timing-function:  var(--ease-standard);\n\n    /* ── The hairline bridge (R.W4 Lane A / A1) ──\n     * Surfaces the R.W3 `--card-edge` mint (:root below — owned THERE, this is\n     * a pure consume) as a Tailwind color key so every Z2 in-plate card writes\n     * the first-class `border-card-edge` utility instead of a magic\n     * `border-[var(--card-edge)]` reach (DESIGN.md §Idioms NOT used). */\n    --color-card-edge: var(--card-edge);\n\n    /* ── The material-ladder bridges (T.W3-1 — D1; owned in :root below) ──\n     * `bg-well` / `bg-stage` / `text-on-stage-chrome` etc. resolve the rung-2\n     * WELL and rung-4 STAGE tokens as first-class utilities so no consumer\n     * ever re-mints a well alpha or a raw black/white stage by hand again\n     * (the T-CM-4 parallel-mint pathology, closed at the token). */\n    --color-well: var(--well-bg);\n    --color-stage: var(--stage);\n    --color-on-stage-chrome: var(--on-stage-chrome);\n\n    /* ── The φ-ladder spacing bridges (S.W4-8) ──\n     * Surface the :root φ rungs (owned below) as Tailwind spacing keys so\n     * consumers write `py-phi-3` / `pb-phi-4`, never `py-[1.618rem]`\n     * arbitrary literals (AboutPane's former re-hardcode of the ladder —\n     * design-docs-about P3). */\n    --spacing-phi-0: var(--phi-0);\n    --spacing-phi-1: var(--phi-1);\n    --spacing-phi-2: var(--phi-2);\n    --spacing-phi-3: var(--phi-3);\n    --spacing-phi-4: var(--phi-4);\n}\n\n/* Project tokens (layout, surfaces).\n *\n * Dock layout — THE DOCK-ATOP BAND LAW (T.W6 · T-31, owner-verbatim: \"our\n * core layout should have the dock atop, with the card/scene area on the\n * bottom below that\"; supersedes B.W1's Proposal-B fixed overlay):\n *   --dock-h      = icon-btn + vertical padding + border  (the band's floor)\n *   --dock-inset  = the shell's top padding (the band's breathing room)\n *   --dock-gap    = the DESIGNED gap between the two bands (the grid row-gap)\n *   --content-max-h = the cap on the pane container's height\n *\n * .app-layout is a TWO-BAND GRID (`auto 1fr`): the dock band (<nav>, in-flow,\n * static) sits ATOP as row 1; the scene band (<main>) sits BELOW as row 2.\n * The former simulation — a position:fixed overlay + a --dock-total\n * padding-top reservation + a load-bearing z-dock — RETIRED TOGETHER: cards\n * cannot composite over the dock BY CONSTRUCTION (they live in another grid\n * row), so the paint order no longer depends on any z-index chain (the P9\n * phantom-utility single point of failure the owner's shot reproduced).\n * Zero z-index arms; portaled menus keep their own chrome z. The former\n * 0–1px arithmetic clearance at short viewports dies behind the designed\n * --dock-gap row-gap. At ultra-wide aspect ratios the dock keeps its\n * pinned-at-top read — the band IS the top, in-flow (the Proposal-B delta,\n * re-confirmed in-band). */\n/* The per-view accent (S.W7 · W7-4): registering `--accent-view` with a real\n * <color> type makes it INTERPOLABLE — but the transition lives ONLY on the\n * bounded accent-painting scope (DockViewSelect's trigger), NEVER on `:root`.\n * The former `--view-hue-shift` <number> registration + `:root` transition\n * (R.W4 B2) taxed the WHOLE document per sweep frame (every inherited\n * custom-property consumer re-resolved 60×/s — design-dock-shell P1-7); the\n * W3-7 mechanism decision retires it: the per-view tokens are resolved\n * JS-side (library gamut-map + contrast guard, useViewAccents) and SNAP on\n * the root; the sweep survives where the accent actually paints. PRM: the\n * global reduced-motion guard (animations.css) neutralises the scoped\n * transition like any other. */\n@property --accent-view {\n    syntax: \"<color>\";\n    inherits: true;\n    /* The same pre-hydration literal as `--accent-live` below — @property\n     * initial values must be computationally independent (no var()). */\n    initial-value: oklch(0.632 0.214 13.5);\n}\n\n:root {\n    /* ── Project theme tokens ──\n     * These override glass-ui defaults for project-specific aesthetics.\n     */\n\n    /* ── The font root (R.W3 Lane A / A1 — the three-voice law) ──\n     * Fraunces is the atlas/display voice; Plus Jakarta Sans the body voice;\n     * Fira Code the readout/annotation voice. The override lands on the SOURCE\n     * token glass-ui's `@theme` bridge inlines (`--font-stack-display`), so\n     * every `.font-display` / `.text-display-*` rung — glass-ui-compiled and\n     * demo-authored alike — resolves Fraunces BY CONSTRUCTION (never via the\n     * dead `--font-display` runtime var, never via `!important` overrides).\n     * Fraunces' single brand source is the SELF-HOSTED @font-face set in\n     * demo/color-picker/index.html (W2-3/LS-6 — the Google-Fonts network\n     * actor retired; the glass-ui corpus carries no Fraunces); Jakarta +\n     * Fira load as real faces from the corpus import above. \"Fraunces\n     * Fallback\" is the size-adjust-tuned Georgia (the bounded ink gate's\n     * reflow-free landing face). */\n    --font-stack-display: \"Fraunces\", \"Fraunces Fallback\", serif;\n\n    /* ── The accent axis (R.W3 Lane A / A2 — the app's chromatic voice) ──\n     * `--accent-live` is the contrast-guarded LIVE picked color, written by\n     * App.vue from the library `safeAccentColor` path (the same SAFE_ACCENT_KEY\n     * computation the dock consumes — ONE color-resolution path, inv-N-3).\n     * The value below is only the pre-hydration fallback: chromatically true to\n     * the default picked color (lab(92% 88.8 20)), guarded to the light-scheme\n     * lightness so first paint is never ink. `--primary` re-points onto it —\n     * the interactive layer speaks the picked color, not `--foreground` — and\n     * the glass frost carries the live temperature at low strength through the\n     * EXISTING `--glass-tint-source`/`--glass-tint-strength` knob (no new\n     * surface, no demo-local glass recipe). */\n    --accent-live: oklch(0.632 0.214 13.5);\n\n    /* ── The per-view accent (S.W7 · W7-4 — navigation reads chromatically,\n     * gamut-guaranteed). The former CSS relative-color derivation\n     * (`oklch(from var(--accent-live) l c calc(h + shift))`) trusted the\n     * browser's gamut clamp — measured false: the clamp bends L per hue\n     * (mix 2.74:1 / generate 2.77:1 failed the 3:1 graphics floor) and at\n     * C≈0 all nine rotations collapsed to one gray. ONE resolver path now:\n     * viewSchema.ts declares each view's `accentHueShift`; `useViewAccents`\n     * resolves each token THROUGH THE LIBRARY (rotate → low-C floor →\n     * Ottosson gamut-map to the cusp → L re-guard → WCAG ≥3:1) and writes\n     * `--accent-view-<id>` × 9 + this `--accent-view` + `--seal-ink` as\n     * static root tokens per accent change. The declaration below is only\n     * the pre-hydration fallback (picker's shift is 0°, so falling back to\n     * the live axis is chromatically true). The view-switch hue sweep lives\n     * on the BOUNDED trigger scope (see the @property registration above) —\n     * never a `:root` transition. `--primary` rides the view accent; the\n     * glass frost keeps reading `--accent-live` (the plate temperature\n     * stays the picked color). */\n    --accent-view: var(--accent-live);\n    --primary: var(--accent-view);\n    --primary-foreground: var(--background);\n    --glass-tint-source: var(--accent-live);\n    --glass-tint-strength: 4%;\n\n    /* ── The accent-aware focus register (R.W3 Lane C / C5, D8) ──\n     * glass-ui's `--focus-ring-shadow` recipe reads ONE retint knob\n     * (`--focus-ring-color`, its sole reader — scale-paper.css). Re-point it\n     * onto the accent axis so every keyboard focus ring — slider thumbs,\n     * select triggers, rail items, readout cells — paints the live picked\n     * color's contrast-guarded voice instead of neutral ink. The `.dark` arm\n     * re-pins the same knob below (glass-ui's dark arm would otherwise win\n     * the cascade back to gray). */\n    --focus-ring-color: var(--accent-live);\n\n    /* ── The hairline mint (R.W3 Lane A / A5 — depth law 4, glassy hairlines) ──\n     * ONE `--card-edge` mint, owned here; R.W4 is a pure consumer. Every card\n     * hairline mixes from `--foreground` so it stays in-house in both schemes —\n     * never an opaque foreign-hue border. See demo/DESIGN.md §Depth. */\n    --card-edge: color-mix(in oklab, var(--foreground) 12%, transparent);\n\n    /* ── The gamut ink/paper pairs (R.W3 Lane B / B1 — out-of-gamut as a\n     * designed state, treatment §COLOR clause 1 verbatim). The overlay's\n     * truth-line contour + visibly-clipped hatch must stay legible over EVERY\n     * (s,v) region of the spectrum plate — a single-ink hatch disappears on\n     * dark/saturated substrate (prototype-proven) — so the vocabulary is an\n     * ink pair (from --foreground) and a paper pair (from --background),\n     * applied per contour segment by the field's own luma (the shared\n     * spectrumLuma helper, flip at 0.5). The overlay canvas resolves all four\n     * via a computed-style probe; the hatch is drawn twice, registered.\n     *\n     * T.W6-1 (T-6, the R5 recalibrated band, re-judged on the W3 plate):\n     * the W5-8 \"subtle\" register was an explicit owner recalibration UP —\n     * the old 9%/12% hatch + 28%/50% edge + 1px stroke measured 33/23\n     * per-255 luma delta on the live plate (sub-texture). The R5 candidate\n     * center (22% ink) was judged on the pre-W1 wash-era plate; on the W3\n     * WELL ground it re-measures 46/38 — under the O-19 floor (≥59 L /\n     * ≥45 D), so the floor rules the mix: 30% ink / 36% paper measures\n     * 61/51 on the live W3 plate at desktop + 390 (intensity moves, the\n     * architecture stands). The tile geometry (period 6 / weight 1.25) is the\n     * sole register — the former paint-consumer that mirrored it is retired. */\n    --gamut-edge:        color-mix(in oklab, var(--foreground) 45%, transparent);\n    --gamut-hatch:       repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,\n                           transparent 0 4.75px,\n                           color-mix(in oklab, var(--foreground) 30%, transparent) 4.75px 6px);\n    --gamut-edge-paper:  color-mix(in oklab, var(--background) 65%, transparent);\n    --gamut-hatch-paper: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg,\n                           transparent 0 4.75px,\n                           color-mix(in oklab, var(--background) 36%, transparent) 4.75px 6px);\n\n    /* ── The alpha transparency checker (S owner-ruling 2026-07-05) ──\n     * ONE recipe, one home: the idiomatic transparency ground every alpha-\n     * carrying ramp/well composes UNDER its color layer via the background\n     * shorthand — `background: <ramp>, var(--alpha-checker)`. 8px squares\n     * (16px tile), two-tone in the house neutrals: --background + a quiet\n     * --foreground mix, so both schemes stay in-material by construction\n     * (dark gets a dark checker, never a white flash). The token carries its\n     * own position/size — it is a complete background LAYER; compose it via\n     * `background:`, not `background-image:`. Consumers: the picker's alpha\n     * slider track (ComponentSliders), the gradient editor bar + stop wells\n     * (GradientStopEditor). */\n    --alpha-checker: repeating-conic-gradient(\n            color-mix(in oklab, var(--foreground) 14%, var(--background)) 0% 25%,\n            var(--background) 0% 50%\n        ) left top / 16px 16px;\n\n    /* ── THE MATERIAL LADDER, rungs 2 + 4 (T.W3-1 — SYNTHESIS §2 D1) ──\n     * Rung-2 WELL: the recessed in-plate fixture — an OPAQUE tone-step of the\n     * plate, NO backdrop-blur (nothing live sits behind an in-plate fixture;\n     * blurring the aurora THROUGH the host is the mud generator, t-card-material\n     * RC-3). The tone-step is the D1 bracket default: 8% `--foreground` into\n     * `--card`, oklab, judged inside [6%, 10%] at the O-7 census. INTERIM demo\n     * mint — the producer `.glass-well`/`--glass-bg-well` rung is packet P3;\n     * this token swaps onto it at the adopt event (BOOKED, T.W3 §BOOKS).\n     * Consumers: `.dashed-well`, PaletteCard (+skeleton), the gradient\n     * perceived-space plate + stop chip, VersionHistoryDrawer rows, the mix\n     * result plate — the six parallel hand-mints D1 retires. */\n    --well-bg: color-mix(in oklab, var(--card) 92%, var(--foreground) 8%);\n\n    /* Rung-4 STAGE: the named near-black pair for photographic/media grounds\n     * (extract image stage, caption veils, on-stage chrome). Scheme-INVARIANT\n     * by design — a photograph's ground does not flip with the theme — and\n     * warm stone, per Q18's ratified neutral family (raw #fff/#000 survive\n     * only inside color-math ramps). Replaces the raw `bg-black`/`bg-white/NN`\n     * literals (t-card-color-census §1.E; CC-7). */\n    --stage: rgb(28 25 23);\n    --on-stage-chrome: rgb(233 230 226);\n}\n\n/* ── THE CONSOLE WELL (T.W4-4 · D5 · Q4 \"The well.\") ──\n * The rung-2 WELL as a seated sub-card CLASS — ONE home for the console\n * species (the picker's sliders console + ConfigSliderPane, the app's\n * second slider population — the M-34 population clause), so no consumer\n * ever re-mints the recipe. Opaque tone-step of the plate (--well-bg), the\n * ONE hairline (--card-edge), the panel radius rung; NO backdrop-blur\n * (nothing live behind an in-plate fixture — C5's material ruling), NO\n * cartoon shadow (depth law 2: the plate already casts the pane's rung).\n * INTERIM demo class — swaps onto the producer `.glass-well` rung when\n * packet P3 ships (BOOKED, T.W3 §BOOKS). */\n.console-well {\n    background: var(--well-bg);\n    border: 1px solid var(--card-edge);\n    border-radius: var(--radius-panel);\n}\n\n:root {\n\n    --shadow-color: var(--foreground);\n\n    /* PROJECT OVERRIDE: the demo's identity surface shadow is a bold pop-art\n     * cartoon offset. glass-ui's default --shadow-card is the soft --shadow-md\n     * and its --shadow-cartoon is a subtle 3px/8% rung. Override the cartoon\n     * rung to the demo's intensity and route --shadow-card through it, so\n     * `shadow-card` consumers and explicit `shadow-cartoon` consumers render\n     * one cartoon language — no fourth ad-hoc shadow recipe. */\n    --shadow-cartoon: 8px 8px 0px 0px color-mix(in srgb, var(--shadow-color) 80%, transparent);\n    --shadow-cartoon-hover: 10px 10px 0px 0px color-mix(in srgb, var(--shadow-color) 85%, transparent);\n    --shadow-card: var(--shadow-cartoon);\n    --shadow-card-hover: var(--shadow-cartoon-hover);\n\n    /* PROJECT OVERRIDE: monospace fonts for Select and DropdownMenu triggers\n     * (glass-ui defaults to inherit). */\n    --select-font: var(--font-mono);\n    --dropdown-menu-font: var(--font-mono);\n\n    /* ── The display-weight pin (T.W4-1 — D2 \"non-bold\"; the P10 booked swap) ──\n     * The owner's non-bold edict for the display voice, pinned at :root the\n     * same shape as `--font-stack-display`: glass-ui's `text-display-*`\n     * utilities hardcode `font-weight: 600` (and `text-heading` 700) with no\n     * token seam (t-title-typography F8), so every demo title surface carries\n     * `font-weight: var(--type-weight-display)` on its OWN class list. When\n     * P10's weight tokenization ships, the producer utilities read this same\n     * knob and the per-surface declarations retire (BOOKED, verify-first). */\n    --type-weight-display: 400;\n\n    /* ── The ornament layer (T.W4-5 · D8 · Q3b) ──\n     * \"Higher z than all\" reads as the top of the CONTENT stack (the ruled\n     * Q3b default): above both pane cards and every in-card fixture (the\n     * picker CardHeader's z-10 included), BELOW floating chrome — the dock/\n     * menus band starts at --z-header 35. Under the flush seat the bead\n     * never enters the chrome band in paint, so the two readings of \"all\"\n     * never conflict (D8). A NAMED tier, never source-order accident. */\n    --z-ornament: 20;\n\n    /* ── Layout tokens ── (T.W6 · T-31 dropped --dock-total: the band grid\n     * owns the reservation structurally — no padding arithmetic simulates\n     * the dock's space, so there is nothing left to derive) */\n    --dock-border-width: 3px;\n    --dock-padding-y: 0.75rem;\n    /* --dock-h is the control/separator basis (it shadows glass-ui's identical\n     * :root value, which feeds `--dock-separator-height: --dock-h × 0.5`); it\n     * is NOT the band floor — inflating it would grow the producer's dock\n     * separator by construction (probed 27.5→36px). The band floor is the\n     * dedicated `--dock-band-min-h` below. */\n    --dock-h: calc(var(--size-icon-btn) + var(--dock-padding-y) + var(--dock-border-width));\n    /* ── The dock-band floor (T.W8 · P9-R2/WR-9/T-57 — the reflow cure) ──\n     * The .dock-band is row 1 of the `auto 1fr` shell grid; its height tracked\n     * the dock's content, so idle-collapse↔re-expand SHRANK then GREW the band\n     * (measured: EXPANDED band 71.4px, COLLAPSED 65.4px → the centred\n     * .pane-container shifted 99.7↔102.7 = +3.0px every cycle, both schemes —\n     * the T-57 downshift the owner redded). The T-31 band law now EXTENDS to\n     * the collapse↔expand AXIS: the band floors at the TALLEST (expanded) state\n     * so the pill/seal/action-bar morph renders INSIDE a constant band by\n     * construction (the shorter collapsed seal centres in the reserved box) —\n     * zero z-index arms, never a margin patch. The reserve = the control atom\n     * (`--size-icon-btn` 40px) + the dock chrome the expanded pill adds above\n     * it (measured 31.4px = block-padding 16 + border 3 + control-vs-icon 6 +\n     * the inline-flex line-box descent 6.4), rounded to 2rem (72px ≥ 71.4). It\n     * RETIRES to the producer `--dock-pill-h` rung when it ships (communiqué\n     * §1.9c); the O-15/t31 band-height invariance probe across the morph is the\n     * drift guard until then. */\n    --dock-band-min-h: calc(var(--size-icon-btn) + 2rem);\n    --dock-inset: 1rem;\n    --dock-gap: 1rem;\n    /* The scene band's own height IS the honest cap (row 2 of the shell\n     * grid resolves it by construction); the desktop/ultra-wide designed\n     * clamps below override it. */\n    --content-max-h: 100%;\n\n    /* ── The pane clamp ladder (R.W3 Lane A / A4 — U32) ──\n     * The cards GROW then clamp, handled generally: `--pane-min` is the floor,\n     * `--pane-max` the per-card ceiling, `--pane-gap` a fluid φ-stepped gutter.\n     * The GRID owns the clamp via the `min()` container formula below — pane\n     * shells never self-clamp (the 10 `lg:max-w-desktop-pane` forks are\n     * deleted; shells are `w-full` only). No per-width media staircase.\n     * OWNER RULING 2026-07-05 (card-width): 44rem → 32rem (~27% off — \"about\n     * 1/3 smaller, maybe a bit less\"); the floor drops 30rem → 25rem to stay\n     * below the new ceiling. 32rem over 30rem by eye: at 30rem the About\n     * card's Components labels wrap mid-word (\"a* (Green-Red)\" breaks). */\n    --pane-min: 25rem;\n    --pane-max: 32rem;\n    --pane-gap: clamp(0.5rem, 1.25vw, 1.618rem);\n\n    /* Shared min-width for dropdown/select menu panels (was 5 ad-hoc widths). */\n    --menu-min-w: 11rem;\n\n    /* App-shell horizontal padding (D.W4 Lane A §4.1 / §5.3 drift) — was a\n     * silent 1rem literal coupled between .app-layout's `padding: … 1rem …`\n     * and .pane-container's `max-width: calc(… + 2rem)`. Both now read this\n     * token so the coupling is explicit and survives a future tightening. */\n    --app-padding-x: 1rem;\n\n    /* ── The φ ladder (S.W4-8 — promoted from Markdown.vue's private scoped\n     * block; design-docs-about P3). 1rem base, neighbours a factor of\n     * φ ≈ 1.618 apart. The docs body rhythm (Markdown.vue) AND the About\n     * pane's sectional padding read the same rungs — one ladder, never a\n     * re-hardcoded arbitrary value. */\n    --phi-0: 0.382rem; /* base ÷ φ² */\n    --phi-1: 0.618rem; /* base ÷ φ  */\n    --phi-2: 1rem; /*     base      */\n    --phi-3: 1.618rem; /* base × φ  */\n    --phi-4: 2.618rem; /* base × φ² */\n}\n\n/* Desktop: tighter dock margins.\n * The aspect law (R.W3 Lane A / A4): the desktop grammar — tighter dock,\n * capped content height, the dual grid below — fires on width AND landscape.\n * A portrait tablet ≥ 1024px wide runs the single-slot mobile grammar with the\n * relaxed dvh-based `--content-max-h` (the D6-03 portrait pathology: two\n * columns marooned mid-screen on a 1080×1750 slab). */\n@media (min-width: 1024px) and (min-aspect-ratio: 1.1) {\n    :root {\n        --dock-inset: 0.5rem;\n        --dock-gap: 0.5rem;\n        --content-max-h: clamp(34rem, 86dvh, 52rem);\n    }\n}\n\n@media (min-aspect-ratio: 21 / 9) {\n    :root {\n        --content-max-h: clamp(30rem, 62dvh, 38rem);\n    }\n}\n\n/* D.W4 Lane A: .palette-card-grid containment hints colocated into\n * PaletteCardGrid.vue. (The `.palette-tab-content` cascade died with\n * PaletteDialog.vue — the dialog-era shell excised at T.W0-3, CC-6.) */\n\n\n/* PROJECT OVERRIDE: dark-mode shadow tuning only (R.W3 Lane A / A3).\n * The dark COLOR ladder is glass-ui 4.2's stepped warm dark-material ladder\n * (page L4 → card L16 → hover L22 → border L34, hue 24–34 throughout) —\n * consumed as shipped. The demo's former hue-217/224 `--popover`/`--border`/\n * `--input` re-pins were the LONE cool hues in the warm house (U26's \"foreign\n * hue\" navy hairline) and FOUGHT the producer's ladder; they are deleted, not\n * retuned — zero borders compute in the 200–240 navy band. */\n.dark {\n    /* PROJECT OVERRIDE — the dark-scheme cartoon caster is a SHADOW, not a\n     * highlight (T.W8 · P6-R1/WR-5/T-53, the caster re-cut). At :root\n     * `--shadow-color: var(--foreground)` — correct in light (the foreground\n     * IS the stone ink), but in dark `--foreground` is the CREAM ink\n     * (#e9e6e2 ≈ srgb 0.914 0.902 0.886), so every shadow-card/shadow-cartoon\n     * consumer cast a LIGHT 8px slab: a \"shadow\" up to +88/255 BRIGHTER than\n     * the ground it shades (measured 143–161/255 over grounds of 55–92/255 —\n     * the owner's re-sighted \"artifact at the edges of the top border of\n     * cards\", NOT the T-45 blur class: bisection-proven filter-independent).\n     * Pin the caster ink to the STONE form (the light arm's own value) so the\n     * caster stays a scheme-true SHADOW in both schemes; the dark-tuned alpha\n     * (50/55%) below now paints stone-over-bright-field = honest depth. The\n     * cartoon OFFSET register (8px/0-blur stamp, D1) survives UNTOUCHED — this\n     * is the ONE knob (`--shadow-color`), never a producer fork (the P3 book\n     * stands for its own smear class). Pole A of the P6-B1 register bracket;\n     * the owner rules which register dark speaks in. */\n    --shadow-color: color(srgb 0.11 0.098 0.09);\n\n    /* Lighter cartoon shadows in dark mode; --shadow-card / --shadow-card-hover\n     * resolve through these via the var() reference set in :root. */\n    --shadow-cartoon: 8px 8px 0px 0px color-mix(in srgb, var(--shadow-color) 50%, transparent);\n    --shadow-cartoon-hover: 10px 10px 0px 0px color-mix(in srgb, var(--shadow-color) 55%, transparent);\n\n    --shadow: hsl(0 0% 45%);\n\n    /* The accent-aware focus register holds in dark (R.W3 Lane C / C5):\n     * glass-ui's dark arm re-declares --focus-ring-color to warm gray; re-pin\n     * it to the accent axis (`--accent-live` is contrast-guarded per scheme). */\n    --focus-ring-color: var(--accent-live);\n}\n\n/* ── The text-selection ink (T.W8 · P11-R1/T-24) ──\n * Every stylesheet (demo + glass-ui) shipped ZERO `::selection` rules, so a\n * text selection painted the browser's DEFAULT BLUE — the single foreign\n * accent in a bespoke terracotta/brick derived-atmosphere app, over the warm\n * ground in BOTH schemes. The cure keys the selection to the live-accent +\n * foreground TOKENS (never a hardcoded hue), the same per-scheme derived\n * discipline the ink-walk cure applies: the highlight is the live picked\n * accent at a legible alpha (`--accent-live` is contrast-guarded per scheme);\n * the ink rides the scheme `--foreground`, which flips light↔dark by\n * construction. `::-moz-selection` carries Firefox. A semi-transparent tint\n * (never opaque) keeps the underlying ink legible over any surface. */\n::selection {\n    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-live) 32%, transparent);\n    color: var(--foreground);\n}\n::-moz-selection {\n    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-live) 32%, transparent);\n    color: var(--foreground);\n}\n\n/* Underline tab variant — active tab gets a colored bottom border.\n * Apply this class to the Tabs root; set --active-tab-color via :style.\n * MARKER (A.W2 / coordination/Q.md §3): this is a demo-side override of a\n * reka-ui attribute selector. It is retired once glass-ui ships a Tabs\n * `underline` variant; until then the override stays. */\n.underline-tabs button[role=\"tab\"][data-state=\"active\"] {\n    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--active-tab-color, var(--primary));\n    border-radius: 0;\n}\n\n/* MARKER (S owner-ruling 2026-07-05, alpha-checker lane): restatement of\n * glass-ui's OWN spectrum-range rule, which its SOURCE declares (Slider.vue —\n * `background: transparent; backdrop-filter: none; -webkit-backdrop-filter:\n * none; box-shadow: none`) but whose DIST minification drops the UNPREFIXED\n * `backdrop-filter: none` leg, keeping only `-webkit-backdrop-filter: none`.\n * Chromium does not implement the -webkit- alias (computed reads empty), so\n * in Chrome the `.glass-liquid-fill` register's backdrop blur stays LIVE on\n * every spectrum range — washing the track under it (it blurred the ramps\n * before; it liquefied the alpha checker into a flat wash, which is how it\n * was caught). NOT a fork — a byte-level restatement of producer intent,\n * scoped to the exact producer selector. Retire when the glass-ui dist keeps\n * the unprefixed leg (reported; the W8 /slider consume is the checkpoint). */\n.glass-slider[data-variant=\"spectrum\"] .slider-range {\n    backdrop-filter: none;\n    -webkit-backdrop-filter: none;\n}\n\n\n/* D.W4 Lane A: .touch-gate-* cluster colocated into ComponentSliders.vue's\n * unscoped <style>; .pane-scroll-fade colocated into PaneHeader.vue's unscoped\n * <style> (alongside the --pane-scroll consumers). (The `.palette-tab-content`\n * data-state cascade died with PaletteDialog.vue at T.W0-3, CC-6.) */\n\n/* Slug pill — the user/palette slug chip recipe, shared across the dock menus,\n * the admin users panel, and the slug bar (was copy-pasted at 5+ sites).\n * Consumers set `color` / `border-color` per-instance via :style. */\n.slug-pill {\n    @apply text-mono-small font-bold px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full border;\n}\n\n/* Base styles for compatibility */\n@layer base {\n    * {\n        border-color: var(--border);\n    }\n    body {\n        /* W2-2 (T.W2, supersedes the W6-1 base-stop ground): THE GRADIENT\n         * GROUND — the body boots inside the derived-palette GRADIENT, the\n         * field's whole material (never the deepest stop as a flat slab —\n         * t-aurora-boot F-2's dark-mud + luminance leap). The template is\n         * FIXED (it mirrors the producer's paletteToCssGradient geometry:\n         * 135deg, 4 stops); only the registered per-stop `<color>` properties\n         * `--saved-bg-0..3` move (written by useAtmosphere's sink + the\n         * index.html fouc-guard boot script — boot/ground.ts is the record\n         * of truth). Each stop rides the :root 200ms transition below, so a\n         * discrete pick breathes into the new family in OKLab (F-12) and the\n         * boot crossfade blends like-with-like (F-4). `--saved-bg` (the base\n         * stop) stays as the solid fallback var; first-ever visits get the\n         * scheme-honest constant pair from the boot script (F-6). */\n        background-color: var(--saved-bg, var(--background));\n        background-image: linear-gradient(\n            135deg,\n            var(--saved-bg-0, var(--saved-bg, var(--background))) 0%,\n            var(--saved-bg-1, var(--saved-bg, var(--background))) 33%,\n            var(--saved-bg-2, var(--saved-bg, var(--background))) 67%,\n            var(--saved-bg-3, var(--saved-bg, var(--background))) 100%\n        );\n        color: var(--foreground);\n    }\n    :root {\n        /* W2-2 — the ground's material clock: each registered `--saved-bg-*`\n         * stop (registered in index.html, pre-paint) interpolates as a\n         * `<color>` — OKLab by CSS Color 4's default — over 200ms decelerate.\n         * The rAF re-derive under a continuous drag outruns this (one write\n         * per frame → the transition restarts at the fresh value, visually\n         * the live tracking the drag already had — W2-5's byte-identity\n         * clause holds); only DISCRETE picks (swatch click, palette apply)\n         * ride the full 200ms breath. PRM: a color crossfade is a state\n         * change, not motion — kept under reduced motion by design. */\n        transition:\n            --saved-bg-0 200ms var(--ease-decelerate),\n            --saved-bg-1 200ms var(--ease-decelerate),\n            --saved-bg-2 200ms var(--ease-decelerate),\n            --saved-bg-3 200ms var(--ease-decelerate),\n            --saved-bg 200ms var(--ease-decelerate);\n    }\n}\n\n/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n * THE A11Y MODALITY SUPPORT LAYER (U.W-A11Y · U-F57 + U-F58)\n * ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n *\n * The app aesthetic is glass/translucent (aurora / blob / veil / glass), so\n * each user-preference modality gets a DESIGNED fallback — never a blanket\n * system-color override (E-3: a designed fallback per modality, born-RED gated\n * BR-5..BR-8/BR-10/BR-11). ZERO forced-colors / prefers-contrast /\n * prefers-reduced-transparency / @media print rules existed before this block\n * (VERIFIED grep, count 0). The demo-side support lands HERE; the\n * producer-primitive halves (GlassDock / Button / Select / veil / WatercolorDot /\n * GooBlob under forced-colors + reduced-transparency, forced-color-adjust:none on\n * the producer COLOR surfaces, the focus `outline`, the Slider aria-valuetext\n * prop-through) are the BH RELAY addendum (E-2) — a demo-only pass leaves the\n * producer glass invisible in WHCM, so the relay is load-bearing.\n *\n * COLOR-SURFACE ROSTER (the two-tier `forced-color-adjust` policy below reuses\n * it): the surfaces whose whole PURPOSE is to show a color — the actual content\n * of a color tool — must survive WHCM's system-color substitution. The chrome\n * (buttons, labels, borders, the dock) adopts system colors by default (`auto`).\n */\n\n/* ── The named color-DISPLAY surfaces (demo-owned) ──────────────────────────\n * The one roster, reused by @media (forced-colors) + @media print so the \"keep\n * the colors\" set is declared ONCE. `canvas` covers the spectrum gamut overlay,\n * the atmosphere field, and the producer blob leaf in one leaf-level rule\n * (canvases paint raster color by construction). */\n\n/* ── U-F57 · @media (forced-colors: active) — the two-tier policy (BR-5) ──────\n * WHCM strips author colors + box-shadow. A blanket substitution would DESTROY\n * the color content the tool exists to show, so:\n *   tier 1 — `forced-color-adjust: none` on the color-DISPLAY surfaces (they\n *            keep their real colors);\n *   tier 2 — the CHROME stays at the UA default `auto` (adopts Canvas /\n *            CanvasText / ButtonFace / ButtonText / Highlight) so it is visible\n *            + operable;\n *   plus  — the U-F25 focus bind: box-shadow rings vanish in WHCM, so restore a\n *            real `outline` (system `Highlight`) on every operable control. The\n *            normal-register dual-contrast ring is the controls lane's\n *            focus-ring.css recipe; THIS block is only the WHCM `outline`\n *            fallback (the one register the shadow ring cannot survive). */\n@media (forced-colors: active) {\n    /* tier 1 — color-display surfaces keep their colors */\n    canvas,\n    .spectrum-picker,\n    .gamut-overlay,\n    .atmosphere-canvas,\n    [data-glass-field-canvas],\n    .gradient-rail,\n    .rail-handle,\n    .readout-rail,\n    .swatch-row > *,\n    .generate-swatch,\n    .shadow-swatch,\n    .goo-blob-canvas,\n    .watercolor-swatch,\n    .glass-slider[data-variant=\"spectrum\"] .slider-range,\n    [data-color-surface] {\n        forced-color-adjust: none;\n    }\n\n    /* the U-F25 focus bind — a real outline where the shadow ring cannot paint.\n     * `:where(...)` keeps the specificity at 0 so a control's own focus rule\n     * (or the controls lane's focus-ring.css) still wins the normal register;\n     * here the outline is the WHCM-only affordance. */\n    :where(\n            a[href],\n            button,\n            [role=\"button\"],\n            [role=\"combobox\"],\n            [role=\"tab\"],\n            [role=\"slider\"],\n            [role=\"menuitem\"],\n            [role=\"option\"],\n            input,\n            select,\n            summary,\n            .rail-handle,\n            .rail-remove-chip,\n            [tabindex]:not([tabindex=\"-1\"])\n        ):focus-visible {\n        outline: 2px solid Highlight;\n        outline-offset: 2px;\n    }\n}\n\n/* ── U-F57 · @media (prefers-contrast: more) — the elevated-contrast layer (BR-6)\n * ONE override token set (not per-component): the low-contrast decorative tints\n * (the U-F12 warm-brown muddiness) DROP, borders thicken toward full-ink, and\n * the muddiest text token rises to the foreground floor. The glass calms so the\n * text floor holds over it. */\n@media (prefers-contrast: more) {\n    :root,\n    .dark {\n        /* drop the decorative glass tint + calm the material so text floors hold */\n        --glass-tint-strength: 0%;\n        --glass-level: 0.1;\n        /* borders + hairlines to a high-contrast weight */\n        --border: color-mix(in oklab, var(--foreground) 78%, var(--background));\n        --card-edge: color-mix(in oklab, var(--foreground) 55%, transparent);\n        /* raise the muddiest low-contrast text to the ink floor */\n        --muted-foreground: color-mix(in oklab, var(--foreground) 88%, var(--background));\n    }\n    /* thicker operable-chrome borders (one weight bump, not per-component).\n     * The `.app-layout` prefix lifts specificity to 0,2,0 so the bump beats the\n     * producer SFC-scoped hairline on the in-shell glass surfaces. */\n    .console-well,\n    .app-layout .glass-resting,\n    .app-layout .console-well,\n    .slug-pill,\n    [role=\"tab\"] {\n        border-width: 2px;\n    }\n}\n\n/* ── U-F57 · @media (prefers-reduced-transparency: reduce) — opaque fallback (BR-7)\n * The veil / dock glass / popover glass drop translucency for an OPAQUE surface.\n * The producer-sanctioned blur lever is `--glass-level: 0` (glass-ui's\n * `--glass-blur-*: blur(calc(radius * var(--glass-level)))` chain → blur(0); the\n * SAME lever the producer's own timeline-rail reduced-transparency rule uses),\n * set at :root so it INHERITS through portaled overlays (popovers/menus in\n * <body>). The opaque background is ONE fallback token (`--surface-reduced-opaque`,\n * the same in-plate material the veil approaches — coordinates with U-F10). The\n * `!important` on backdrop-filter/background is the deliberate MODALITY ESCAPE\n * (the whole intent is to forcibly reduce transparency) — it beats producer\n * SFC-scoped rules (`.glass-resting[data-v-*]`, specificity 0,2,0) without a\n * per-surface specificity fight; it is scoped to this media block only. */\n@media (prefers-reduced-transparency: reduce) {\n    :root,\n    .dark {\n        --glass-level: 0;\n        --glass-tint-strength: 0%;\n        --surface-reduced-opaque: var(--card);\n    }\n    /* kill residual backdrop-filter (blur(0) still carries a saturate leg) +\n     * the demo T-45 oversampled carrier's blur */\n    .glass-resting,\n    .glass-floating,\n    .glass-wash,\n    .veil-surface,\n    [data-surface=\"veil\"],\n    .pane-wrapper::before,\n    .pane-wrapper > div::before {\n        backdrop-filter: none !important;\n        -webkit-backdrop-filter: none !important;\n    }\n    /* opaque surface — nothing shows through, whatever the residual filter */\n    .glass-resting,\n    .glass-floating,\n    .glass-wash,\n    .veil-surface,\n    [data-surface=\"veil\"] {\n        background-color: var(--surface-reduced-opaque, var(--card)) !important;\n    }\n}\n\n/* ── U-F58 · @media print — the palette IS a printable artifact (BR-11) ───────\n * A color tool's output is a printable palette: the swatches + hex/space labels\n * printed with faithful ink, the glass/aurora/blob chrome hidden, ink-economical\n * (white ground, ink text, no shadows/blur). `print-color-adjust: exact` +\n * `forced-color-adjust: none` on the color surfaces make the browser honor the\n * actual swatch colors instead of dropping backgrounds for ink economy — for a\n * color tool the color IS the content. */\n@media print {\n    /* hide the decorative + interactive chrome */\n    .atmosphere-canvas,\n    .goo-blob-wrapper,\n    .goo-blob-canvas,\n    .dock-band,\n    nav[aria-label=\"Application navigation\"] {\n        display: none !important;\n    }\n    /* ink-economical ground */\n    body {\n        background: #fff !important;\n        background-image: none !important;\n        color: #000 !important;\n    }\n    * {\n        box-shadow: none !important;\n        backdrop-filter: none !important;\n        -webkit-backdrop-filter: none !important;\n        text-shadow: none !important;\n    }\n    /* plates print as clean ruled boxes */\n    .glass-resting,\n    .console-well,\n    .veil-surface,\n    [data-surface=\"veil\"] {\n        background: #fff !important;\n        border: 1px solid #000 !important;\n    }\n    /* the color content prints with faithful ink (the whole point) */\n    .spectrum-picker,\n    .gradient-rail,\n    .rail-handle,\n    .swatch-row > *,\n    .generate-swatch,\n    .shadow-swatch,\n    .watercolor-swatch,\n    [data-color-surface] {\n        forced-color-adjust: none;\n        -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact !important;\n        print-color-adjust: exact !important;\n    }\n}\n",
