      "sha256": "a3eed0573edaaa4900fb0fddfab23418aa855a6292876f124ac51dc197ee7d63",
      "encoding": "utf8",
      "content": "/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n * shell.css — the app-shell LAYOUT surface (W43 · RF-15 §b 5 split from\n * style.css). ARCHITECTURE §1 styles home: foundation.css owns global\n * reset/tokens/material/focus primitives; THIS file owns the shell's layout\n * class rules — the dock-atop band grid, the pane container/wrappers, the\n * [data-layout] display witnesses, and the T-45 pane-card oversampled-blur\n * seat. All layout TOKENS (--dock-*, --pane-*, --content-max-h, …) stay in\n * foundation :root; this file consumes them. Loaded via foundation's\n * `@import \"./shell.css\"`.\n * ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */\n\n/* ── App layout — THE DOCK-ATOP BAND LAW (T.W6 · T-31) ──\n * Two-band grid: the dock band (row 1, auto) sits ATOP as structure the\n * layout OWNS; the scene band (row 2, 1fr) sits below behind the designed\n * --dock-gap row-gap. The retired trio (see the token doc-comment above):\n * the fixed overlay, the --dock-total padding reservation, the load-bearing\n * z-dock. Occlusion of the dock by any card is impossible by construction —\n * grid rows do not overlap and no z-index is minted anywhere in the shell. */\n.app-layout {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-rows: auto 1fr;\n    row-gap: var(--dock-gap);\n    height: 100dvh;\n    width: 100%;\n    position: relative;\n    overflow: hidden;\n    padding: var(--dock-inset) var(--app-padding-x) 0.5rem;\n}\n\n/* The a11y landmarks are the two band rows. <nav> IS the dock band —\n * in-flow, static, centring the pill; --dock-band-min-h floors it at the\n * EXPANDED-pill height so the band never jitters across the dock's\n * collapse↔expand morph (T.W8 · P9-R2/T-57: the former --dock-h floor sat\n * BELOW the expanded pill, so the band grew 6.4px on every re-expand and\n * shifted the scene +3.0px — the reservation now covers the tallest state by\n * construction, the shorter collapsed seal centring in the reserved box).\n * position: relative seats the band-chrome instruments (the W6-6 status\n * lamp). */\n.dock-band {\n    position: relative;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    min-height: var(--dock-band-min-h);\n}\n\n/* <main> (.pane-main) is the scene band: it centres the pane container\n * within row 2 (the centring the flex shell used to do at the layout root —\n * now the band's own job). */\n.pane-main {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    justify-content: center;\n    /* flex-min-size idiom — let the column shrink to its content. */\n    min-height: 0;\n    min-width: 0;\n}\n\n.pane-container {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n    gap: 1rem;\n    width: 100%;\n    /* The GRID owns the clamp (R.W3 Lane A / A4 — U32, \"handled generally\"):\n     * the container grows fluidly with the viewport (minus .app-layout's\n     * horizontal padding, both sides) and clamps at two max-size cards plus\n     * the gutter (≈ 1050px — 32rem × 2 + 1.618rem, the 2026-07-05 owner-ruling\n     * clamp). Equal columns always; no shell self-clamps. */\n    max-width: min(\n        calc(100vw - var(--app-padding-x) * 2),\n        calc(var(--pane-max) * 2 + var(--pane-gap))\n    );\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    position: relative;\n    max-height: var(--content-max-h);\n    min-height: 0;\n}\n\n/* The pane slots are size containers: in-card sizing rides `cqi` (container\n * queries — structurally immune to the viewport-variant kill class), never\n * `vw`. Display type rungs are the named exception (viewport-fluid clamps). */\n.pane-wrapper {\n    container-type: inline-size;\n}\n\n/* W6-4 (S.W6) — the SLOT-owned cross-pane layer: the LEFT slot (the picker +\n * its corner-breaking hero-blob ornament) paints above the right pane, so the\n * bead's overlap strip is never buried under the About card (the S-4 burial —\n * both glass Cards are z-auto stacking contexts, so DOM order alone painted\n * the LATER right pane over the left pane's overflowing ornament). Grid items\n * take z-index directly (no positioning needed); portaled overlays are\n * unaffected; ZERO per-instance z-index on the ornament itself (the\n * no-z-hacks law — the slot assigns the layer). */\n.pane-wrapper--left {\n    z-index: 1;\n}\n\n/* MOB-1 (T round-4 — the C-5/D8-1 adjudication landed) — THE LAYOUT DISPLAY\n * WITNESSES key on [data-layout], the single-truth stamp App.vue sets on\n * .app-layout from `isDesktop` (= width AND landscape). The CSS witness IS the\n * JS witness: a portrait tablet ≥ 1024px wide (aspect < 1.1) stamps\n * data-layout=\"mobile\", so the mobile slot shows and the desktop wrappers hide\n * BY CONSTRUCTION — the retired D6-03 portrait pathology needed a width-only\n * `lg:hidden` display exception here; the stamp dissolves it. The v-if\n * single-mount (App.vue X6) is the primary gate; these are the aspect-correct\n * defensive witnesses + the CI emission canary (scripts/ci/css-emission-probe.mjs,\n * re-pointed off the lg:* utilities onto these rules). They are intentionally\n * UN-media'd — the JS drives the breakpoint, so a media wrapper would\n * re-introduce the width-only disagreement the stamp exists to retire. */\n[data-layout=\"mobile\"] .pane-slot-mobile {\n    display: flex;\n}\n[data-layout=\"desktop\"] .pane-wrapper--left {\n    display: flex;\n}\n[data-layout=\"desktop\"] .pane-wrapper--right {\n    display: block;\n}\n/* The mobile pane switcher (Dock.vue's PaneSegmentedControl) is mobile-grammar\n * only — hidden on desktop, shown on the portrait band so BOTH panes stay\n * reachable at 1024×1366 (the width-only `lg:hidden` it replaced marooned the\n * second pane there). */\n[data-layout=\"desktop\"] .dock-mobile-panes {\n    display: none;\n}\n\n/* The dual grid fires on width AND landscape (the aspect law — see the\n * desktop :root block above; portrait keeps the single-column grammar). */\n@media (min-width: 1024px) and (min-aspect-ratio: 1.1) {\n    .pane-container {\n        gap: var(--pane-gap);\n    }\n    .pane-container--dual {\n        /* Equal columns always (the kept 1fr↔1fr invariant), with the floor\n         * explicit: no card ever renders below `--pane-min` on the dual\n         * grid. */\n        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(var(--pane-min), 1fr));\n    }\n}\n\n/* ═══ T-45 · THE PANE-CARD OVERSAMPLED-BLUR SEAT (T.W6.5 Lane M · the\n * BOOKED-SWAP demo interim; root = producer, P3 rider) ═══════════════════\n *\n * THE DEFECT (t33-audit-13, ROOT FOUND BY BISECTION — t33-research §6.8):\n * the pane card's OWN `backdrop-filter: blur(8px) saturate(1.4)`\n * edge-samples the bright aurora beyond the card's border box (the spec\n * clips the backdrop INPUT at the border box, so the kernel edge-clamps)\n * and smears it inward ≈ one blur radius; the rounded clip then cuts the\n * band unevenly at the corner arcs — the owner's \"strange clipping\n * artifacts on the borders of these cards\". Card filter off → rim GONE;\n * header-veil toggles change nothing.\n *\n * THE CURE CLASS (the oversampled-pseudo idiom): the blur moves onto a\n * layer whose sample region OVERSHOOTS the visible edge by 2× the blur\n * radius, and whose OUTPUT is clipped back to the card's rounded box —\n * the edge-clamp smear falls entirely in the clipped-away band.\n *\n * THE SEAT (why the pane WRAPPER, not the card's own pseudo): the producer\n * ladder already claims BOTH card pseudos (`.glass-resting::before` = the\n * specular catch-light, `::after` = grain + rim — material.css), so an\n * on-card pseudo would fork the ladder (forbidden — the root cure is the\n * producer's); and most pane cards ARE their own scroll containers, where\n * an absolutely-positioned carrier would scroll away with the content and\n * inflate the scrollable overflow. The seat is therefore the pane card's\n * DIRECT WRAPPER (a static box the card fills by construction): the\n * `.pane-wrapper` slot for the root-Card panes, the one-deep wrapper div\n * for the wrapped panes (the picker's `.pane-shell`, Extract/Config).\n * `clip-path` clips hit-testing too, so the overshoot band can never\n * intercept a pointer. The `:not()` arm keeps the carrier SINGULAR during\n * a mixed pane swap (both structures transiently co-mounted in one slot).\n *\n * TOKEN-FIRST, ZERO FORKED VALUES: the carrier reads the SAME\n * `--glass-blur-resting` the `.glass-resting` rung consumes (ladder.css),\n * so `--glass-level`, the W55 bright-bucket, and the reduced-transparency\n * escape (`--glass-level: 0` → blur(0)) retune it in lockstep — every\n * producer escape is inherited by construction, no media-arm restatement.\n *\n * RETIREMENT: the producer-root cure is the BOOKED P3-family rider\n * (letters/GLASSUI-T-ASKS.md §P3/P10 riders — the oversampled-pseudo AT\n * THE LADDER, relayed `92136ab5` on tranche/BG, walked at W7\n * verify-at-cut). This whole block dies the day that lands — never a demo\n * fork of the ladder, a booked-swap interim. */\n@supports selector(:has(*)) {\n    .pane-wrapper:has(> .glass-resting),\n    .pane-wrapper:not(:has(> .glass-resting)) > div:has(> .glass-resting) {\n        position: relative;\n    }\n\n    /* UNPREFIXED backdrop-filter ONLY (the producer's own authoring law —\n     * glass-ui ladder.css authors the bare form and lets Lightning CSS\n     * inject the `-webkit-` companion). Hand-authoring the pair here made\n     * the demo's OWN minifier collapse it to the prefixed form alone (the\n     * exact unprefixed-leg-dropped class the spectrum-range MARKER above\n     * documents), which computes `none` in Chromium — probed live on the\n     * built bundle. */\n    .pane-wrapper:has(> .glass-resting)::before,\n    .pane-wrapper:not(:has(> .glass-resting))\n        > div:has(> .glass-resting)::before {\n        content: \"\";\n        position: absolute;\n        inset: calc(-2 * var(--glass-blur-resting-radius, 8px));\n        pointer-events: none;\n        backdrop-filter: var(--glass-blur-resting);\n        clip-path: inset(\n            calc(2 * var(--glass-blur-resting-radius, 8px))\n                round var(--radius-card)\n        );\n    }\n\n    /* The card's own filter dies where the carrier speaks for it — same\n     * material (one token), sampled wide, clipped true. */\n    .pane-wrapper > .glass-resting,\n    .pane-wrapper > div > .glass-resting {\n        backdrop-filter: none;\n    }\n}\n",
