      "encoding": "utf8",
      "content": "/* Fonts loaded via <link> tags in index.html to avoid render-blocking @import */\n\n/* Project-specific font aliases */\n.fraunces {\n    font-family: var(--font-display);\n    font-optical-sizing: auto;\n}\n\n.fira-code {\n    font-family: var(--font-mono);\n}\n\n/* Shared single-line caption recipe — `.section-label` (glass-ui typography)\n * extended with muted half-opacity and a one-line clamp. Consumed by the\n * control-bar components (gradient / mix / generate). The standard `line-clamp`\n * drives modern engines; `-webkit-line-clamp` + `-webkit-box` remain the\n * Safari support floor. */\n.section-subtitle {\n    font-family: var(--font-mono);\n    font-size: var(--type-caption);\n    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--muted-foreground) 50%, transparent);\n    overflow: hidden;\n    display: -webkit-box;\n    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;\n    -webkit-line-clamp: 1;\n    line-clamp: 1;\n}\n\n/* `.pastel-rainbow-text` EXCISED (S.W5-7 · Q4 RATIFIED EXCISE 2026-07-05;\n * the `--accent-live` ramp alternative NOT taken): the fixed six-hue candy\n * ramp failed contrast at every stop over the light header wash (≈1.1–1.5:1),\n * ignored the per-view accent axis, and was the page's only rainbow moment —\n * decoration, not information. The three consumers (PalettesPane heading,\n * DockViewSelect palettes entry, PaletteDialog header) speak ink. */\n\n/* The ONE loading-ink recipe (S.W5 Lane A / W5-1 — the `ec1b200` register,\n * modernized): every skeleton surface in the app reads this single muted-ink\n * family through glass-ui's `--skeleton-glass-bg` seam — one `color-mix`,\n * both schemes, opaque enough to read as SHADOW against the field, never as\n * content. The `--skeleton-shimmer-tint` line is the letter-L9 producer seam\n * (the sheen joins the same ink family once glass-ui's `::after` reads it).\n * Consumers: ShadowPalette + PaletteCardSkeleton (both `bg-well`),\n * AdminListSkeleton + the admin tag-chip shadows (resting plate).\n *\n * E1-R2 (T.W8 remediation_1): the former `color-mix(muted-foreground 22%,\n * muted)` recipe was NOT certified against its ground — in dark it landed ≈\n * `--well-bg` (probed ΔL 0.007, seg-vs-well 1.02:1), collapsing the ghost to a\n * featureless slab. The ink is now a CERTIFIED tone-step OF the well ground\n * itself: a fixed φ-ish fraction of `--foreground` mixed into `--well-bg`, so\n * the block is guaranteed a bounded ΔL from the well in BOTH schemes by\n * construction (darker than the well in light, lifted above it in dark — the\n * scheme-adaptive direction falls out of the token, no per-scheme fork), and\n * the genesis \"muted blocks\" read as BLOCKS against every neutral skeleton\n * ground (well ≈ resting plate). Low-chroma by construction (both `--well-bg`\n * and `--foreground` are near-neutral), so the muted-family character holds. */\n.skeleton-ink-register {\n    --skeleton-ink: color-mix(in oklab, var(--well-bg), var(--foreground) 15%);\n    --skeleton-glass-bg: var(--skeleton-ink);\n    --skeleton-shimmer-tint: color-mix(in srgb, var(--muted-foreground) 24%, transparent);\n}\n\n/* The SPECIMEN ink walk (S.W5-1's `specimen` register, FINALLY consumed —\n * T.W3-2 · D9): a low-chroma hue rotation around the live accent (fixed 36°\n * steps, C clamped to 0.12) mixed INTO the ink base so the ghost stays\n * shadow-first, per-segment via `--i`. Lifted here from PaletteCardSkeleton's\n * scoped block the day it gained a second consumer (DESIGN.md's\n * global-utility rule): the ShadowPalette true-empty ghost (STILL) reads it\n * as fill; the developing skeleton's strip seams read it through glass-ui's\n * `--skeleton-glass-bg`. Guarded: engines without relative-color calc() keep\n * the plain ink base (the recipe never falls to transparent). */\n.specimen-seg {\n    --specimen-ink: var(--skeleton-ink);\n}\n@supports (color: oklch(from red calc(l) c calc(h + 36deg))) {\n    .specimen-seg {\n        --specimen-ink: color-mix(\n            in oklab,\n            var(--skeleton-ink) 78%,\n            oklch(from var(--accent-live) l 0.12 calc(h + var(--i, 0) * 36deg))\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/* Dashed inset well — the recessed container that collects an in-progress set\n * of colors (the mix \"Selected\" tray, the current-palette editor). Both sites\n * used `.dashed-well` as a never-defined phantom (inv-N-7); this mints the\n * intended affordance in house tokens: a dashed-bordered, faintly-recessed\n * column that visually groups its swatch row + label, echoing the dashed\n * add-swatch button each well already contains. */\n.dashed-well {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    gap: 0.625rem;\n    padding: 0.75rem;\n    /* R.W4 Lane A / A1 — hairline law 4: the well's dashed edge reads the ONE\n     * `--card-edge` mint (in-house, scheme-stable), never a `--border` fork. */\n    border: 1.5px dashed var(--card-edge);\n    border-radius: var(--radius-card);\n    /* T.W3-1 (D1 rung-2 WELL; supersedes the S-20 glass recipe — R8): an\n     * in-plate fixture is an opaque TONE-STEP of its host plate, never a\n     * second pane of glass — the ONE `--well-bg` token, NO backdrop-blur\n     * (blurring the aurora through the host is the mud generator, RC-3).\n     * The dashed edge ALONE carries the in-progress semantics; the chip\n     * cartoon rung stays. */\n    background: var(--well-bg);\n    box-shadow: var(--shadow-cartoon-sm);\n}\n\n/* THE SEATED SEARCH FIELD (T.W3-3 · T-12 — THE REGISTER LAW: fields on paper\n * wear paper; fields on glass stay glass). glass-ui's `.input-bar` recipe is\n * dock furniture — the FLOATING chrome rung (80/88%-α glass + blur(13px) +\n * a 24rem dock cap + a baked mono voice). Seated in a pane BODY it is the one\n * floating-glass element in a cartoon-grammar column (t-search-tabs §1-3):\n * over a flat plate the blur has nothing to blur, the dark roast reads darker\n * than its own plate, and the cap rags the bar 78px short of its siblings at\n * 1440 AND 768 (t-mobile F-7). This opt-in re-seats the bar on the MATERIAL\n * LADDER as the Z2 in-plate fixture it is (DESIGN.md § Surfaces):\n *\n *   fill    — the ONE rung-2 `--well-bg` tone-step, NO backdrop-blur (RC-3);\n *   edge    — the drawn `--card-edge` ink hairline (the dashed-well's solid\n *             sibling — hairline law 4, ONE edge mint);\n *   stamp   — `--shadow-cartoon-sm`, the chip-scale elevation PaletteCard rides;\n *   measure — the dock cap dies: a seated field runs its host column (ASK-C);\n *   voice   — content-class (the `.input-bar-field` rule below).\n *\n * INTERIM DEMO SEAT — a consumer opt-in on the producer recipe (unlayered, so\n * it wins over the `@layer components` recipe by layer order — the exact\n * mechanism the producer's own `bare` rung proved), NEVER a recipe fork.\n * BOOKED SWAP (T.W3 §BOOKS \"W3-3 interim search seat\"): dies onto glass-ui's\n * P3 seated field-chrome rung — GLASSUI-T-ASKS ASK-D (`variant=\"seated\"`),\n * with ASK-B (the font seam) + ASK-C (the cap seam) — at the adopt event. */\n.search-seated {\n    background: var(--well-bg);\n    backdrop-filter: none;\n    border: 1.5px solid var(--card-edge);\n    box-shadow: var(--shadow-cartoon-sm);\n    max-width: none;\n}\n\n/* Compose, never replace: the producer's focus ring joins the stamp (the\n * unlayered base box-shadow above would otherwise silently beat the layered\n * `.input-bar:focus-within` ring). */\n.search-seated:focus-within {\n    box-shadow: var(--shadow-cartoon-sm), var(--focus-ring-shadow);\n}\n\n/* Voice = CONTENT-CLASS (T-12): a prose search field speaks its plate's text\n * voice; the producer's baked `--font-mono` (`components.css:235`, ASK-B's\n * seam target) is a statement about CSS-literal readouts, not prose. Mono\n * stays an EXPLICIT per-field opt-in (SearchFilterBar's color input keeps it\n * by class; identifier fields opt back in the same way). */\n.search-seated .input-bar-field {\n    font-family: inherit;\n}\n\n/* The gold ADMIN-identity icon ink (S.W7-1 consume / W7-7 dedup home) — the\n * ONE demo-side gold icon recipe, lifted here because its consumers span\n * components (the Dock.vue wax-seal ink + DockViewSelect's trigger/menu\n * icons; scoped copies were byte-identical twins, god-module census §2.1).\n * The fuller \"ONE gold/admin shimmer primitive\" consolidation stays the\n * filed glass-ui letter L15 ask. */\n.gold-shimmer-icon {\n    color: var(--color-gold);\n    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 2px color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-gold) 30%, transparent));\n}\n\n/* Swatch-row list idiom (R.W4 Lane B / B1) — shared by the three swatch\n * TransitionGroups (CurrentPaletteEditor, MixSourceSelector,\n * MixResultDisplay): dots pop in/out on the enter/exit family with\n * scale-only geometry, neighbours reflow on the family move class, and the\n * leaving dot is lifted out of flow so the row closes smoothly. A shared\n * recipe (3 consumers) per DESIGN.md's global-utility rule. */\n.swatch-row {\n    --vj-enter-y: 0px;\n    --vj-enter-scale: 0;\n}\n.swatch-row > .vj-enter-leave-active {\n    position: absolute;\n}\n\n/* THE GUARDED LETTERFORM RAMP recipe (T.W6 · W6-4 — Q5 RULED, owner-verbatim:\n * \"Only palettes should be rainbow--the letterforms dropdown and the title\";\n * T-43 owner-CONFIRMS). The ONE recipe for the exactly-TWO consume sites\n * (DockViewSelect's \"Palettes\" entry + PalettesPane's title letterforms) —\n * never a scoped twin (the S.W7-7 lesson). Stops are the THREE root tokens\n * `boot/useViewAccents` writes from the ONE resolver\n * (`@composables/color/palettes-ramp` — derived from the live accent,\n * gamut-guarded, WCAG ≥4.5:1 text-floor); the guard's output IS O-14's T-10\n * referent. C3-ledger: the sanctioned exception to the nav ink law (Q18).\n * Fallbacks = the resolver's own pre-first-write class of value (the\n * `--accent-view` @property initial family), overwritten at first resolve. */\n.palettes-ramp-text {\n    background-image: linear-gradient(\n        90deg,\n        var(--palettes-ramp-0, oklch(0.632 0.214 333.5)),\n        var(--palettes-ramp-1, oklch(0.632 0.214 13.5)),\n        var(--palettes-ramp-2, oklch(0.632 0.214 53.5))\n    );\n    -webkit-background-clip: text;\n    background-clip: text;\n    color: transparent;\n}\n",
