      "encoding": "utf8",
      "content": "# Value 88-SFC Component Workflow Matrix\n\nDate: 2026-07-29\nStatus: FORMATION-ONLY; historical D/L/C evidence remains 218/264, while the\n2026-07-30 supplemental packet closes specification coverage only\nPhysical denominator: committed and live `demo/**/*.vue` census at `e01d0065`\n\n## 1. Reconciliation rule\n\nThe physical denominator is 88 SFCs. The live authority ledger reports:\n\n- 72/88 component rows complete;\n- 218/264 exact and hash-banked D/L/C axes;\n- 16 incomplete rows and 46 unbanked axes.\n\nThe isolated committed snapshot contains an older ledger state with only ten incomplete rows. It is not current truth. This matrix binds the live 72/88 and 218/264 cut. A historical workflow record saying `completed`, a present file, or this planning row does not bank an axis.\n\nEvery physical SFC has a distinct workflow ID below. No component may borrow a sibling’s browser receipt or D/L/C adjudication. Shared parents may coordinate a route sweep, but each child records its own job, protagonist, hierarchy, interaction/paint ownership, state matrix, and terminal disposition.\n\n## 2. Per-component workflow contract\n\nEvery `VC-###` workflow performs, in order:\n\n1. source/parent/child/style/state/DI/test/route/consumer graph census;\n2. route job and protagonist statement;\n3. D design challenge under Golden Glass, Breath of Life, and Movement of Momentum;\n4. L library-grain challenge: KEEP/FOLD/MOVE/SPLIT/PRUNE, module-child filename de-duplication, export and consumer proof;\n5. C implementation challenge: async, cleanup, error, loading, empty, offline, auth/Admin, ownership, and inaccessible-state proof;\n6. isolated prototype or measurement if needed; prototypes never land as product source;\n7. in-app Browser matrix: desktop, 390×844, short landscape, keyboard, reduced motion, forced colors, RTL, and sampled animation frames;\n8. independent re-read, exact D/L/C hashes, validator bank, then wave admission.\n\nGlobal visual gates inherited by all 88 rows:\n\n- semantic heading and landmark hierarchy;\n- cards only where grouping earns a surface;\n- coherent spacing and deliberate dividers;\n- controls name their effect and expose focus;\n- interaction owners do not masquerade as paint owners;\n- removable decoration has a measured purpose;\n- measured-chroma signature belongs to the Value subject, not generic glass chrome;\n- loading, empty, error, offline, auth, and Admin are distinct states rather than silent emptiness.\n\n`ADJ` means the live ledger marks the row adjudicated. `BANK` means exact D/L/C are hash-banked. `OPEN(DLC)` and `OPEN(D)` are current live deficits.\n\n## 3. Core, palette, and picker workflows\n\n| Workflow | Physical SFC | Job / protagonist | Live D/L/C | Formation wave and terminal direction |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| VC-001 | `demo/color-picker/App.vue` | Route shell; the chosen color is protagonist | ADJ | V.U1 shell boundaries; SPLIT route scenes, KEEP composition root |\n| VC-002 | `demo/color-picker/ErrorBoundary.vue` | Make a failed scene recoverable | BANK | V.U1; KEEP only if it catches app/route-owned failures |\n| VC-003 | `demo/color-session/ColorSpaceSelector.vue` | Change the mathematical interpretation of color | ADJ | V.U3; KEEP semantic control, PRUNE decorative selector chrome |\n| VC-004 | `demo/color-session/color-chips/PreviewRamp.vue` | Show ordered tonal change | BANK | V.U3; KEEP measured ramp, FOLD duplicate chip paint |\n| VC-005 | `demo/color-session/color-chips/PreviewStrip.vue` | Compare compact color samples | BANK | V.U3; KEEP comparison, prove forced-colors text equivalent |\n| VC-006 | `demo/palettes/BrowsePane.vue` | Discover public palettes | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); SPLIT offline/error from empty |\n| VC-007 | `demo/palettes/PalettesPane.vue` | Manage the viewer’s palettes | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); central policy, explicit auth/offline |\n| VC-008 | `demo/palettes/admin/AdminPane.vue` | Seat privileged palette operations | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); gate before rendering data state |\n| VC-009 | `demo/palettes/browser/admin/AdminAuditPanel.vue` | Review immutable moderation evidence | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); KEEP audit chronology, hide unauthorized existence |\n| VC-010 | `demo/palettes/browser/admin/AdminFlaggedPanel.vue` | Triage reported palettes | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); KEEP action provenance, explicit queue states |\n| VC-011 | `demo/palettes/browser/admin/AdminListItem.vue` | Present one actionable admin record | OPEN(DLC) | V.U4; independent full workflow required |\n| VC-012 | `demo/palettes/browser/admin/AdminListSkeleton.vue` | Preserve admin-list geometry during load | OPEN(DLC) | V.U4; prove useful, reduced-motion safe, or PRUNE |\n| VC-013 | `demo/palettes/browser/admin/AdminNamesPanel.vue` | Adjudicate proposed names | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); KEEP queue semantics, explicit refusal |\n| VC-014 | `demo/palettes/browser/admin/AdminTagsPanel.vue` | Adjudicate palette tags | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); KEEP taxonomy work, policy-gate |\n| VC-015 | `demo/palettes/browser/admin/AdminUsersPanel.vue` | Administer users | ADJ | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); fix auth/offline-as-empty |\n| VC-016 | `demo/palettes/browser/admin/PaginationBar.vue` | Navigate an admin result window | OPEN(DLC) | V.U4; prove pagination against actual collection semantics |\n| VC-017 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/CurrentPaletteEditor.vue` | Edit the current palette’s identity/content | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); KEEP local ownership, prevent policy bypass |\n| VC-018 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/PaletteCard/ActionFeedback.vue` | Report one card action outcome | OPEN(DLC) | V.U4; merge with owned action if redundant |\n| VC-019 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/PaletteCard/PaletteCard.vue` | Make one palette legible and actionable | BANK | V.U4; KEEP specimen hierarchy, reduce generic card chrome |\n| VC-020 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/PaletteCard/PaletteCardMenu.vue` | Expose policy-valid palette commands | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); FILTER actions through policy |\n| VC-021 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/PaletteCard/PaletteCardMeta.vue` | State authorship/status without stealing focus | OPEN(DLC) | V.U4; prove every metadata field |\n| VC-022 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/PaletteCard/PaletteCardSwatches.vue` | Show the palette itself as card protagonist | BANK | V.U4; KEEP measured chroma, forced-colors equivalent |\n| VC-023 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/PaletteCard/PaletteRenameInput.vue` | Rename one owned palette | OPEN(DLC) | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); local validation and refusal |\n| VC-024 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/PaletteCardGrid.vue` | Lay out a browsable palette collection | OPEN(DLC) | V.U4; own responsive density and collection states |\n| VC-025 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/PaletteCardSkeleton.vue` | Preserve palette-card geometry while loading | BANK | V.U4; KEEP only with distinct loading semantics |\n| VC-026 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/PaletteColorStrip.vue` | Compactly expose a palette’s color order | BANK | V.U4; KEEP chroma signature, accessible fallback |\n| VC-027 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/ShadowPalette.vue` | Preview a pending palette transformation | BANK | V.U4; KEEP only as labeled provisional state |\n| VC-028 | `demo/palettes/browser/card/SwatchHoverMenu.vue` | Act on a specific swatch | BANK | V.U4; keyboard/touch parity, popup ownership |\n| VC-029 | `demo/palettes/browser/dialog/FlagReportDialog.vue` | Submit a moderated report | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); explicit auth/error/success |\n| VC-030 | `demo/palettes/browser/dialog/MigratePalettesDialog.vue` | Explain and execute palette migration | BANK | V.U4 (V.A2 dependency); one migration path, no compatibility fork |\n| VC-031 | `demo/palettes/browser/dialog/VersionHistoryDrawer.vue` | Inspect and recover local palette releases | BANK | V.U4 (V.A2/A3 dependency); rename/version semantics to local releases |\n| VC-032 | `demo/palettes/browser/search/MiniColorPicker.vue` | Add color as a search constraint | BANK | V.U4; KEEP only search-scoped controls |\n| VC-033 | `demo/palettes/browser/search/SearchFilterBar.vue` | Express palette query and filters | BANK | V.U4; SPLIT query state from decorative container |\n| VC-034 | `demo/palettes/browser/search/TagEditPopover.vue` | Edit palette tags in context | OPEN(D) | V.U4; D axis remains open, L/C hash-banked |\n| VC-035 | `demo/palettes/browser/search/UserSortMenu.vue` | Select a meaningful collection ordering | OPEN(DLC) | V.U4; PRUNE options without server semantics |\n| VC-036 | `demo/palettes/browser/slug/PaletteSlugBar.vue` | Show/edit the palette’s durable address | BANK | V.U4 (V.A1 dependency); policy-safe direct-link behavior |\n| VC-037 | `demo/palettes/browser/status/ApiOfflineChip.vue` | Name service unavailability | BANK | V.U4; KEEP as status, never substitute for route error body |\n| VC-038 | `demo/picker/ColorPicker.vue` | Author a color | ADJ | V.U2; KEEP protagonist and local `ActionBarLayer`, dissolve shell/action leakage; V.U3 owns picker descendants |\n| VC-039 | `demo/picker/controls/ComponentSliders/ComponentSliders.vue` | Numerically manipulate color components | BANK | V.U3; KEEP typed controls and direction semantics |\n| VC-040 | `demo/picker/controls/ComponentSliders/ConsoleRail.vue` | Expose diagnostic component values | OPEN(DLC) | V.U3; dev-only proof or PRUNE |\n| VC-041 | `demo/picker/controls/SpectrumCanvas/SpectrumCanvas.vue` | Directly manipulate color in a plane | BANK | V.U3; keyboard alternative and paint/interaction split |\n| VC-042 | `demo/picker/display/ColorComponentDisplay/ColorComponentDisplay.vue` | Read exact component values | OPEN(DLC) | V.U3; own numeric hierarchy, no duplicate readout |\n| VC-043 | `demo/picker/visual/DebugEventLog.vue` | Inspect interaction events during development | OPEN(DLC) | V.U3; dev boundary or PRUNE from product |\n| VC-044 | `demo/picker/visual/HeroBlob.vue` | Embody the authored color | BANK | V.U3; KEEP subject-specific animation with reduced-motion final |\n| VC-045 | `demo/picker/visual/PointerDebugOverlay.vue` | Inspect pointer geometry during development | OPEN(DLC) | V.U3; dev boundary or PRUNE from product |\n\n## 4. Scene and shared-component workflows\n\n| Workflow | Physical SFC | Job / protagonist | Live D/L/C | Formation wave and terminal direction |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| VC-046 | `demo/scenes/ConfigSliderPane.vue` | Configure one generative scene | ADJ | V.U3; KEEP controls subordinate to output |\n| VC-047 | `demo/scenes/about/AboutPane.vue` | Explain Value’s model and provenance | BANK | V.U4; KEEP narrative hierarchy, remove ornamental cards |\n| VC-048 | `demo/scenes/about/ColorNutritionLabel.vue` | Make a color’s measured properties scannable | BANK | V.U4; KEEP distinctive measured-chroma signature |\n| VC-049 | `demo/scenes/about/katex/Katex.vue` | Render mathematical notation | BANK | V.U4; isolate renderer, failure text fallback |\n| VC-050 | `demo/scenes/about/markdown/Markdown.vue` | Render trusted product narrative | ADJ | V.U4; keep bounded syntax and accessible headings |\n| VC-051 | `demo/scenes/atmosphere/AuroraPane.vue` | Generate an atmospheric color field | BANK | V.U3; fix RTL action clipping and motion ownership |\n| VC-052 | `demo/scenes/blob/BlobPane.vue` | Generate an animated color blob | BANK | V.U3; reconcile 200–550ms overlaps and infinite pulse |\n| VC-053 | `demo/shared/ui/EmptyState.vue` | Explain a genuinely empty collection | BANK | V.U4; SPLIT from offline/auth/error |\n| VC-054 | `demo/shared/ui/PaneHeader.vue` | Name the pane job and local actions | BANK | V.U4; semantic heading contract consumed by all routes |\n\n## 5. Shell and dock workflows\n\n| Workflow | Physical SFC | Job / protagonist | Live D/L/C | Formation wave and terminal direction |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| VC-055 | `demo/shell/PaneSegmentedControl.vue` | Switch sibling panes in constrained space | BANK | V.U1; MOVE to true consumer home if shell-only name duplicates child |\n| VC-056 | `demo/shell/PaneSlot.vue` | Seat a route pane without owning its commands | BANK | V.U1; PRUNE ref dispatch and forward-only exposes |\n| VC-057 | `demo/shell/dock/ActionBarToggle.vue` | Open the dock’s route-local action layer | BANK | V.U2; reassess after GenericActionBar deletion |\n| VC-058 | `demo/shell/dock/ActionButton.vue` | Invoke one ColorPicker-local dock action | BANK | V.U2; independently KEEP/challenge; GenericActionBar deletion gives no closure credit |\n| VC-059 | `demo/shell/dock/ActionToolbar.vue` | Seat ColorPicker-local commands | OPEN(DLC) | V.U2; independent open workflow; preserve through ActionBarLayer pending its own result |\n| VC-060 | `demo/shell/dock/ColorInput.vue` | Parse and commit textual color input | ADJ | V.U2 (V.L1 dependency); KEEP failure-explicit typed boundary |\n| VC-061 | `demo/shell/dock/Dock.vue` | Provide persistent navigation/status/input chrome | ADJ | V.U2; SPLIT paint from route command ownership |\n| VC-062 | `demo/shell/dock/DockStatusLamp.vue` | Report current system/session status | BANK | V.U2; remove infinite pulse when status is stable or reduced |\n| VC-063 | `demo/shell/dock/DockViewSelect.vue` | Navigate primary Value views | BANK | V.U2; semantic nav, complete fourteen-route authority |\n| VC-064 | `demo/shell/dock/ParseEchoReadout.vue` | Show parsed input interpretation | OPEN(DLC) | V.U2 (V.L1 dependency); prove user value or dev-only/PRUNE |\n| VC-065 | `demo/shell/dock/layers/ActionBarLayer.vue` | Seat ColorPicker-owned dock commands | BANK | V.U2; KEEP ColorPicker-local layer; fold only proven forward-only relay |\n| VC-066 | `demo/shell/dock/layers/GenericActionBar.vue` | Silent shell-to-pane command proxy | BANK | V.U2 terminal DELETE; no replacement registry/renderer |\n| VC-067 | `demo/shell/dock/layers/SlugEditLayer.vue` | Edit the current palette slug | BANK | V.U2 (V.A1 dependency); route-local ownership and refusal |\n| VC-068 | `demo/shell/dock/menus/MobileMenuDropdown.vue` | Expose navigation/session actions on mobile | BANK | V.U2; restore focus to trigger on Escape |\n| VC-069 | `demo/shell/dock/menus/ProfileSection.vue` | Expose authenticated identity actions | BANK | V.U2 (V.A1 dependency); explicit anonymous/offline/error states |\n\n## 6. Workbench workflows\n\n| Workflow | Physical SFC | Job / protagonist | Live D/L/C | Formation wave and terminal direction |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| VC-070 | `demo/workbenches/extract/ExtractControls.vue` | Configure palette extraction | BANK | V.U3; controls subordinate to source image/result |\n| VC-071 | `demo/workbenches/extract/ExtractPane.vue` | Seat extraction workflow | BANK | V.U3; route-local states and commands |\n| VC-072 | `demo/workbenches/extract/ExtractWorkbench.vue` | Coordinate image-to-palette extraction | BANK | V.U3; KEEP state owner, split renderer leaves |\n| VC-073 | `demo/workbenches/extract/ImageDropZone.vue` | Acquire an image | BANK | V.U3; keyboard/paste/drop/error parity |\n| VC-074 | `demo/workbenches/extract/ImageEyedropper/ImageEyedropper.vue` | Sample color from an image | BANK | V.U3; pointer/keyboard geometry and cleanup |\n| VC-075 | `demo/workbenches/generate/GenerateControls.vue` | Configure palette generation | ADJ | V.U3; KEEP meaningful generator dimensions |\n| VC-076 | `demo/workbenches/generate/GeneratePane.vue` | Generate and save a palette | BANK | V.U3; local seats survive; V.U2 owns only generic relay deletion |\n| VC-077 | `demo/workbenches/gradient/GradientPane.vue` | Author a gradient | OPEN(DLC) | V.U3; add local Reset; DELETE implicit first-palette Seed |\n| VC-078 | `demo/workbenches/gradient/GradientVisualizer/GradientCodeEditor.vue` | Edit canonical gradient text | BANK | V.U3 + V.L1/L2; parse/refusal/inverse proof |\n| VC-079 | `demo/workbenches/gradient/GradientVisualizer/GradientEasingEditor.vue` | Author gradient easing | BANK | V.U3 + V.L3; no Keyframes sampling-policy absorption |\n| VC-080 | `demo/workbenches/gradient/GradientVisualizer/GradientStopEditor.vue` | Author ordered gradient stops | ADJ | V.U3; named buttons, focus, forced-colors distinction |\n| VC-081 | `demo/workbenches/gradient/GradientVisualizer/GradientVisualizer.vue` | Make the gradient the route protagonist | BANK | V.U3; measured-chroma signature, local command surface |\n| VC-082 | `demo/workbenches/gradient/GradientVisualizer/easing/EasingAuthoringStage.vue` | Shape an easing curve | BANK | V.U3 + V.L3; typed curve state, sampled animation frames |\n| VC-083 | `demo/workbenches/gradient/GradientVisualizer/easing/EasingSpecimenStrip.vue` | Compare easing behavior | BANK | V.U3 + V.L3; reduced-motion static comparison |\n| VC-084 | `demo/workbenches/mix/MixAnimationCanvas/MixAnimationCanvas.vue` | Show temporal color mixing | BANK | V.U3; KEEP animation only with timing/cleanup proof |\n| VC-085 | `demo/workbenches/mix/MixConfigBar.vue` | Configure a mix | BANK | V.U3; fold decorative bar into meaningful control group |\n| VC-086 | `demo/workbenches/mix/MixPane.vue` | Mix selected palette colors | BANK | V.U3; local Mix survives; DELETE `copyResult`, `clearSelection`, `MIN_COLORS`, and `canRemoveColor`; removal reaches zero |\n| VC-087 | `demo/workbenches/mix/MixResultDisplay.vue` | Present the mixed color/result | BANK | V.U3; local result Copy/Reset survive; result is protagonist |\n| VC-088 | `demo/workbenches/mix/MixSourceSelector.vue` | Select mix inputs | BANK | V.U3; enforce selection meaning and empty guidance |\n\n## 7. Live incomplete-row closure packet\n\nThe exact sixteen rows requiring new durable work are:\n\n```text\nVC-011 AdminListItem              D/L/C\nVC-012 AdminListSkeleton          D/L/C\nVC-016 PaginationBar              D/L/C\nVC-018 ActionFeedback             D/L/C\nVC-021 PaletteCardMeta            D/L/C\nVC-023 PaletteRenameInput         D/L/C\nVC-024 PaletteCardGrid            D/L/C\nVC-034 TagEditPopover             D only\nVC-035 UserSort