      "content": "# Value Mobile Safari Kronecker audit plan — 2026-08-01\n\n## 0. Status and non-credit boundary\n\n**Status:** `SOURCE-ONLY OWNER MARK / PLAN COMPLETE / INVENTORY EXECUTION RED / SAFARI EXECUTION RED`\n\nThis packet consumes the cross-repository Mobile Safari Kronecker audit law and\nroutes it into the Value owner lane. It is a tranche-development plan. It does\nnot execute the demo, API, Browser, Safari, parser, packages, releases, or\nproduct source. It grants no product, Browser, visual, execution, parser,\npackage, release, API, or constellation-close credit.\n\nThe parser remains **PAUSED**. The existing Value non-parser formation matrix\nremains 11/11 specification-complete, and the parser-law matrix remains 14/34.\nThis new platform-audit denominator is separate: prior formation rows are input\nto its inventory, not Safari evidence.\n\n## 1. Bound authority and source truth\n\n### 1.1 Governing law\n\n| Authority | Coordinate | Disposition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cross-repo Mobile Safari Kronecker audit law | live read-only `/Users/mkbabb/Programming/value.js/docs/tranches/V/megatranche/formation/CROSS-REPO-MOBILE-SAFARI-KRONECKER-AUDIT-LAW-2026-08-01.md`; SHA-256 `2ab310b45b9289b53f5e1993ef870a0ae80cdd12c2856628fa523df85bf3ae5e` | **KEEP** as the audit law |\n| Current root chronology | handoff `2dff32ea448d762554be1e6b77e39a3704613a22546ba2daeb11d5af33a1da6e`; manifest `94ea0053dbd6e1dc4a7c7b976a35c95257a0c12759bf0fdf1cd2c7c34a4afe5c`; checksum file `046c266886c99953fd4e9999f80c6409ce8af029f63a611aa2b24f2dbb1b1a72`; pi handoff `b798fe33ba5ab13c14ca1bfafa78467b6607c2be995579b1b8c190f74cd71822` | chronology only; 6/6 checksum rows independently replayed green; no Value authority or credit inferred |\n| Existing component matrix | `COMPONENT-WORKFLOW-MATRIX-2026-07-29.md`; SHA-256 `3efc8638b765f0cb7bef019ff3d3b6a2f47664b1f66b6b9c6ff3fb9dd301c6a9` | **KEEP** as the 88-workflow identity seed, not Apple-platform evidence |\n| Existing frontend closure | `NON-PARSER-FRONTEND-SPEC-CLOSURE-2026-07-30.md`; SHA-256 `a911162502a5a32cb512c00af266004e1d5d3f56ed2a963256b75caa3ee6c883` | **KEEP** as specification input, not execution evidence |\n| Existing Browser archaeology | `RESEARCH-PASSES-AND-BROWSER-AUDIT-2026-07-29.md`; SHA-256 `df91b6c383e6f2d37c9a69b7b62d70fac04f0e22febdef9c3ec0bc0ae9e00fd5` | **KEEP** as diagnostic negative evidence; **PRUNE** from Safari credit |\n| Non-parser matrix | SHA-256 `717bf1e36e11fb9b702dc95b26be82c26bffce48c9c8a78c8a7cc3bb614435c5` | unchanged at 11/11 specification rows |\n| Parser-law matrix | SHA-256 `244c448a90059002be1194e6a512191c96881a9413ceb021f3b8fe7b62b504a7` | unchanged at 14/34; parser PAUSED |\n| Formation status | SHA-256 `713ae753738af09985f9e5d63e96182b953c4cc62dd8daff1815b1f8e0dae1ea` | unchanged |\n\nThe current root chronology records Keyframes v8 Review A clean/root-inspected\nwith Review B released, Fourier v4w terminal with v4x active, and the parser\npaused. Those are dependency facts only. Active, clean, or released sibling\nwork does not satisfy a Value audit cell.\n\nThe crossrepo-v5 Value owner slot remains `null`. This source-only plan cannot\npopulate it; only a later immutable Value owner admission may do so.\n\n### 1.2 Current source join\n\nThe isolated worktree and live evidence tree both resolve product source to\ncommit `e01d0065fa6c7c80282280566af2b9a4add809bf`. The live tree is nevertheless\ndirty in tranche/documentation surfaces, so its branch tip is not claimed as\nthe complete live truth. The bounded product join found no live dirt under\n`demo`, `src`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `vite.config.ts`, or\n`index.html`.\n\n| Source subject | Current observation | Meaning |\n|---|---:|---|\n| `demo/**/*.vue` physical files | 88 local / 88 live | source identity seed only |\n| ordered SFC path-list SHA-256 | `861e56ef4f78c3f5822f44e707e6e1905d4af39f527b18b879a48cd35379ac19` local/live | path census agrees at the bounded coordinate |\n| ordered SFC content-manifest SHA-256 | `876a9c20d1b10735ea08b5ff15535113d99716c774effdb1f558edc7de6df362` local/live | SFC bytes agree at the bounded coordinate |\n| router source SHA-256 | `2aaa2282b397722cf8cf1e5696412c8a00d3dea6148b615c1206fc152de66aa0` local/live | route declaration source agrees |\n| `.vue` source/declaration edges | 115 observed, including barrel exports | a mount-graph floor, not an instance denominator |\n| demo visual barrel declarations | 25 | export census input; mounted-versus-harness classification remains RED |\n| visual exports in the published package map | 0 observed | must receive an exact package/deployment proof before terminal closure |\n\nThe router uses stub route components while the rendered pane is also selected\nthrough `usePaneRouter`. Therefore a route declaration does not prove the\nmounted scene, state, or component instance. `V.MSK1` and `V.MSK2` must join\nrouter, pane router, shell, conditional templates, teleport targets, and\nexport barrels before freezing any page or instance denominator.\n\n## 2. Exact subject inventory to be closed\n\n### 2.1 Router pages and non-route page surfaces\n\nThe source route identity seed is 14 named paths plus one wildcard redirect\nrule. The wildcard is not counted as a fifteenth page; it owns redirect,\nunknown-path, deep-link, focus, title, and error-fallback cells.\n\n| Class | Exact paths | Required page ownership |\n|---|---|---|\n| public/local authoring | `/`, `/browse`, `/extract`, `/mix`, `/generate`, `/gradient`, `/atmosphere`, `/blob` | each path owns its own route job, protagonist, mounted scene, title, semantic H1, deep link, data/network states, compact/large layout, and component instances |\n| member/authenticated | `/palettes` | anonymous, authenticating, authenticated owner, authenticated other, expired/revoked session, API offline, empty/single/many, private/public, active/trashed, clear/withdrawn moderation, and visible immutable-release states |\n| Admin | `/admin/users`, `/admin/names`, `/admin/audit`, `/admin/flagged`, `/admin/tags` | anonymous/non-admin hiding, admin loading/empty/error/data/action/conflict, direct deep link, refresh, back-forward cache, and stale authority |\n| redirect/error rule | `/:pathMatch(.*)*` -> `/` | unknown path, encoded path, query/hash preservation or refusal, redirect loop refusal, title/focus announcement, and error-boundary behavior |\n\nPage-like surfaces outside the router remain first-class audit subjects. The\nsource census must include `AboutPane`, palette details/history, mobile panes,\ndialogs, drawers, menus, popovers, tooltips, tabs, `VC-002 ErrorBoundary`,\n`VC-037 ApiOfflineChip`, dev-misconfiguration alerts, and any nested workbench\nthat occupies the page protagonist. They receive page matrices when they alter\nthe primary document job; otherwise they receive component-instance matrices\nunder the owning page.\n\nDebug surfaces `VC-043 PointerDebugOverlay` and `VC-045 DebugEventLog`, and the\nphysically present `GenericActionBar`, remain in the current-source census even\nthough formation dispositions route them to deletion. They leave the audit\ndenominator only after an authenticated product coordinate proves their\nabsence. A proposed deletion is not an executed deletion.\n\n### 2.2 Component workflows\n\nEvery physical SFC receives its own workflow. No family row, page screenshot,\nor shared receipt may substitute for a child component.\n\n| Workflow family | Exact rows | Count | Audit rule |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| core, palette, picker, and palette-browser surfaces | `VC-001`–`VC-045` | 45 | one mounted-instance matrix per live mount; unmounted export gets a harness matrix |\n| scenes and shared visual surfaces | `VC-046`–`VC-054` | 9 | page-like scenes also bind route/pane identity |\n| shell, dock, pane, layers, and controls | `VC-055`–`VC-069` | 15 | shell evidence never closes route-local commands or nested layers |\n| extract, generate, gradient, mix, and workbench surfaces | `VC-070`–`VC-088` | 19 | each workbench and child control owns its state and motion matrix |\n| **total** | `VC-001`–`VC-088` | **88** | exact workflow bijection required |\n\nThe sixteen formerly open specification rows—`VC-011`, `VC-012`, `VC-016`,\n`VC-018`, `VC-021`, `VC-023`, `VC-024`, `VC-034`, `VC-035`, `VC-040`,\n`VC-042`, `VC-043`, `VC-045`, `VC-059`, `VC-064`, and `VC-077`—remain\nspecification-closed only. They receive no special execution shortcut.\n\n### 2.3 Exported visual surfaces\n\nThe current 25 demo barrel declarations are:\n\n- `PreviewRamp`, `PreviewStrip`;\n- `AdminUsersPanel`, `AdminNamesPanel`, `AdminAuditPanel`,\n  `AdminFlaggedPanel`, `AdminTagsPanel`;\n- `ColorPicker`, `Katex`, `Markdown`, `PaletteSlugBar`, and `Dock`;\n- `PaletteCard`, `PaletteCardGrid`, `PaletteCardSkeleton`, `ShadowPalette`,\n  `PaletteColorStrip`, and `CurrentPaletteEditor`;\n- `SearchFilterBar`, `UserSortMenu`, and `TagEditPopover`;\n- `FlagReportDialog`, `VersionHistoryDrawer`, `MigratePalettesDialog`, and\n  `ApiOfflineChip`.\n\n`V.MSK2` must classify each declaration as:\n\n1. `MOUNTED`: link every live instance and predicate to its page;\n2. `EXPORTED_UNMOUNTED`: create a production-import harness with exact\n   props/events/slots/variants/defaults and consumer proof;\n3. `NONVISUAL_OR_ALIAS`: prove the alias and bind the canonical visual owner;\n4. `TERMINAL_PRUNE`: prove no current consumer and route the export deletion;\n5. `SOURCE_ABSENT`: only after an authenticated later source coordinate.\n\nThe 25 declarations overlap the 88 SFCs and are never added to 88 as though\nthey were new components. An exported component can require both an instance\nmatrix and an export-contract matrix.\n\n## 3. Kronecker registry\n\nThe future machine-readable registry is governed by:\n\n```text\nK = R x O x P x C x D x V x L x I x X x N x A x T\n```\n\n| Axis | Value-specific domain that must be enumerated |\n|---|---|\n| `R` repository/package | Value source coordinate, demo entry, built artifact coordinate, Glass artifact coordinate, API coordinate, service-worker/static assets, exact CSS/fonts |\n| `O` origin/environment | deployed production-like origin; authenticated isolated local frontend; isolated real API/database; offline fixture; feature/config/auth/storage state |\n| `P` page/route | 14 named paths, wildcard behavior, page-like panes, redirects, aliases, direct links, history and resume transitions |\n| `C` component | each mounted SFC instance, each conditionally duplicated instance, each exported-unmounted harness subject, each dialog/drawer/menu/layer/portal target |\n| `D` device/browser | real iOS Simulator Mobile Safari coordinates, physical iOS where Simulator is insufficient, installed desktop Safari coordinates |\n| `V` viewport/geometry | compact notched iPhone portrait/landscape, large iPhone, iPad portrait/landscape where supported, desktop Safari narrow/standard/wide, 100%/200% zoom, safe areas, software keyboard, container sizes |\n| `L` locale/display | LTR/RTL, long/short copy, locale/number formatting, light/dark, Dynamic Type, forced-colors or exact platform-equivalent proof, display scale |\n| `I` interaction/lifecycle | inactive, initial, active, idle, hover where available, focus, pressed, expanded, dragging, scrolling, editing, validating, submitting, settled, background/resume, rotation, BFCache, unmount/remount |\n| `X` data/auth | absent/null, empty, one, many, large, stale, optimistic, conflict, deleted, private/public, active/trashed, clear/withdrawn, anonymous, authenticating, owner, other, Admin, expired/revoked |\n| `N` network/API | online, cold/warm offline, slow, timeout, aborted, retry, resumed, 401, hidden 404, 409, 412, 429, 5xx, malformed, partial, stale cache, service-worker/CORS/CSP failure |\n| `A` accessibility/input | keyboard-only, touch, trackpad/mouse, VoiceOver, focus order/trap/return, landmarks/name/role/value/live regions, target size, contrast, text zoom, rotor and switch-compatible semantics |\n| `T` time/animation | first paint; 0/120/250/420 ms and animation-specific sampled frames; loading-to-data, open/close, add/remove/reorder, drag, retry, background/resume; reduced-motion immediate/final seating |\n\nThe user-requested state classes map into the registry as follows:\n\n| Requested class | Owning axes | Minimum proof |\n|---|---|---|\n| active / inactive / idle | `I x T` | visible semantics, input response, focus, paint/interaction ownership, settled state |\n| loading / error / empty | `I x X x N x T` | exact copy, live-region behavior, retry/escape path, layout stability |\n| interactive | `I x A x T` | touch and keyboard path, focus, gesture cancellation, disabled/refusal behavior |\n| data | `X x N` | null/empty/single/many/large/stale/conflict/deleted with API provenance |\n| auth | `X x O x N` | anonymous/authenticating/owner/other/Admin/expired/revoked and hidden-existence policy |\n| network | `N x O x T` | online/offline/slow/failure/recovery and service-worker/cache behavior |\n| motion | `T x A` | sampled frames, one semantic motion owner, interrupt/reverse/settle, reduced-motion alternative |\n| accessibility | `A x L x V` | keyboard, VoiceOver, Dynamic Type/zoom, RTL, contrast, landmarks and announcements |\n\nNo state may be called `N/A` because a fixture was inconvenient. A reduction\nis valid only when a machine-readable equivalence proof names the omitted cell,\nthe executed witness, the identical axes, the inapplicability predicate, the\nsource paths that establish it, and a hostile mutation that makes the proof\nfail. The raw Cartesian product is never multiplied into a decorative count\nbefore applicability and equivalence are sealed.\n\n## 4. Per-page and per-component contract\n\nEvery page and every component instance owns all of the following fields:\n\n1. immutable subject ID, source path, export path, mount path, route/pane owner,\n   condition, duplicate-instance key, and teardown owner;\n2. user, single job, protagonist, primary action, secondary actions, refusal\n   path, exact state copy, title, H1, landmarks, and deep-link contract;\n3. props, events, slots, defaults, variants, consumer evidence, API/state/DI\n   inputs, visible output, and terminal `KEEP/FOLD/MOVE/SPLIT/PRUNE`;\n4. responsive and container ownership, safe-area behavior, keyboard occlusion,\n   scrolling owner, overflow, zoom, long-copy, RTL, and Dynamic Type behavior;\n5. keyboard/touch/VoiceOver interaction, focus entry/order/trap/return, target\n   size, contrast, name/role/value, live regions, error association, and\n   destructive confirmation;\n6. active, inactive, idle, loading, empty, error, offline, auth, Admin, data,\n   network, motion, and accessibility applicability with exact fixtures;\n7. animation owner, sampled frame times, interruption/reversal, semantic final\n   state, reduced-motion result, geometry/pixel tolerance, and measurement tool;\n8. API calls, policy decision, CAS/ETag/idempotency inputs, retries, provenance,\n   redaction, stale/conflict behavior, and cleanup;\n9. Glass primitives/styles/fonts used, package graph, paint versus interaction\n   ownership, copied CSS/raw alias/ref-bridge checks, and removal proof;\n10. raw evidence packet IDs for iOS Safari and desktop Safari, defects,\n    remediation coordinate, rerun IDs, reviewer verdicts, and residual risk.\n\nOne page screenshot cannot close its component children. One component harness\ncannot close the component in a page/container/auth/network context. A shared\nshell result cannot close a route-local command. A generic state row cannot\nstand in for component-specific copy or focus behavior.\n\n## 5. Subject-specific design law\n\nThe audit uses the `frontend-design` skill as a formation rubric. Value helps\ncolor practitioners author, compare, generate, transform, save, share, and\ngovern measured color. Its signature must therefore arise from measured chroma,\ntransformation, relationship, and provenance—not generic gradients, glass\ncards, pill controls, or decorative motion.\n\nEvery route/page and every `VC-001`–`VC-088` workflow receives two distinct\ndesign passes:\n\n### Pass D1 — subject-specific brief\n\n- name the user, page/component job, protagonist, decision, and success state;\n- name the measured-color data or provenance that determines palette, tokens,\n  contrast, layout, or motion;\n- define display/body/utility typography, hierarchy, density, spacing,\n  dividers, cards, controls, container behavior, and exact state copy;\n- identify the one memorable signature and the one semantic motion owner;\n- appraise **Golden Glass**, **Breath of Life**, and **Movement of Momentum**\n  with concrete measured-chroma evidence or record a justified refusal;\n- specify loading, empty, error, offline, auth/Admin, reduced-motion,\n  forced-colors/platform-equivalent, RTL, keyboard, VoiceOver, and Dynamic Type.\n\n### Pass D2 — independent critique\n\n- test whether the result could be mistaken for a generic dashboard or stock\n  component library;\n- remove decoration that does not communicate color relationship, state,\n  provenance, affordance, or hierarchy;\n- challenge excessive cards, rounded containers, divider noise, duplicated\n  labels, weak protagonist, generic copy, gratuitous gradients, and motion\n  without state ownership;\n- challenge paint layers that intercept input, hidden focus, unsafe targets,\n  clipped popovers, keyboard occlusion, scroll traps, and reduced-motion drift;\n- return terminal `KEEP/FOLD/MOVE/SPLIT/PRUNE` per concept and exact remediation\n  receiver. It does not edit product source.\n\nThe two passes may share source evidence but not authorial judgment. A family\nbrief may establish vocabulary; it cannot replace the component-specific row.\n\n## 6. Real Apple evidence admission\n\n### 6.1 iOS Simulator Mobile Safari\n\nThe future execution coordinate must record exact macOS host, hardware, Xcode,\niOS runtime, Simulator device type, OS version, UDID, boot state, Mobile Safari\nversion/build, locale, appearance, Dynamic Type, reduced-motion state,\norientation, display scale, software-keyboard state, VoiceOver state, origin,\nfrontend/API/fixture hashes, and automation commit.\n\nRequired device classes are a compact notched iPhone, a large iPhone, and an\niPad in portrait and landscape wherever the product claims support. Rotation,\nsafe areas, keyboard appearance, background/resume, deep links, touch gestures,\nselection, clipboard/share/download, and VoiceOver must be exercised. A\nphysical iPhone/iPad is required for any camera, color-management, GPU,\nmemory-pressure, gesture, share-sheet, or other behavior the Simulator cannot\nfaithfully establish.\n\nAutomation must drive the installed Mobile Safari UI using XCUITest or a\nrecorded Apple UI automation coordinate and retain raw screenshots/video,\naccessibility data, console/network evidence where available, commands, exit\ncodes, and state transitions. Resized Chromium, device emulation, Playwright\nWebKit, a screenshot renderer, or the in-app Browser earns **zero** iOS Safari\ncredit.\n\n### 6.2 Installed desktop Safari\n\nThe future coordinate must record exact macOS, hardware, GPU, display, scale,\ninstalled Safari version/build, Safari settings, automation driver identity,\norigin, frontend/API/fixture hashes, and profile/cache/service-worker state.\n\nIt must exercise narrow, standard, and wide windows; 100% and 200% page zoom;\nlight/dark; reduced motion; keyboard-only; mouse/hover and trackpad; RTL and\nlong copy; Dynamic Type/platform text scaling where applicable; back/forward\ncache; direct deep links; downloads/share/clipboard; storage; service worker;\nconsole; network; memory; layout; and timeline. Playwright WebKit does not\nsubstitute for installed Safari.\n\n### 6.3 Origin, API, and temporary harness\n\nEach platform must run against:\n\n1. an authenticated deployed-origin coordinate;\n2. an authenticated isolated local frontend plus isolated real API/database;\n3. a deterministic offline fixture.\n\nTemporary runtime/test-harness repairs may use unique ports, disposable copied\nconfiguration, fixtures, proxying, or an isolated Docker project/network/volume.\nThey may not mutate permanent product source, packages, existing containers,\nvolumes, or databases. Every repair receipt must include the defect, exact\nbefore identity, disposable fix, commands, images/configs/ports/health checks,\nfrontend and API identities, evidence, teardown, absence proof, and exact after\nidentity. Secrets are never recorded. A checkout byte change requires byte and\nstat restoration proof before its evidence is eligible.\n\n## 7. Raw-first cell packet\n\nEach executed cell writes raw evidence before any summary. Minimum schema:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"cellId\": \"stable Kronecker cell ID\",\n  \"subject\": {\"pageId\": \"...\", \"componentId\": \"VC-...\", \"instanceId\": \"...\"},\n  \"coordinate\": {\"repo\": \"...\", \"origin\": \"...\", \"api\": \"...\", \"fixture\": \"...\"},\n  \"axes\": {\"R\": \"...\", \"O\": \"...\", \"P\": \"...\", \"C\": \"...\", \"D\": \"...\", \"V\": \"...\", \"L\": \"...\", \"I\": \"...\", \"X\": \"...\", \"N\": \"...\", \"A\": \"...\", \"T\": \"...\"},\n  \"setup\": {\"commands\": [], \"environment\": {}, \"beforeIdentity\": \"...\"},\n  \"actions\": [],\n  \"expected\": {\"copy\": \"...\", \"semantics\": \"...\", \"geometry\": \"...\", \"motion\": \"...\"},\n  \"raw\": {\"screenshots\": [], \"video\": [], \"accessibility\": [], \"console\": [], \"network\": [], \"performance\": []},\n  \"result\": \"PASS|FAIL|BLOCKED\",\n  \"defects\": [],\n  \"cleanup\": {\"commands\": [], \"absenceProof\": \"...\", \"afterIdentity\": \"...\"},\n  \"credit\": {\"product\": false, \"browser\": false, \"visual\": false, \"execution\": false, \"release\": false}\n}\n```\n\nThe finalized schema must add exact versioning, content hashes, modes, file\nmembership, units, tolerances, refusal reasons, and producer/consumer\nvalidation. A generated summary cannot authenticate its own raw inputs.\n\n## 8. Ordered waves\n\nAll current activity stops at the plan boundary. The waves below are future\ntranche work and do not authorize product edits.\n\n| Wave | Goal and bounded units | Dependencies | Born-RED gate | Completion and artifacts |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `V.MSK0` authority freeze | bind law, local/live product coordinate, route/SFC/package/export hashes, root chronology, dirty-state exclusions | none | any hash/path/branch ambiguity | `AUTHORITY.json`, source census command receipt, zero-credit status |\n| `V.MSK1` page census | 14 paths, wildcard behavior, aliases/redirects, pane router, title/H1/access/deep links, page-like panes, error/offline/auth/Admin states | `V.MSK0` | route-to-render join incomplete; any public/auth/admin/debug/error surface lacks owner | `PAGE-INVENTORY.json`, route/pane graph, page-policy matrix |\n| `V.MSK2` component/export census | all `VC-001`–`VC-088`, every live mount instance/predicate/duplicate/teleport, 25 barrel declarations, package visual-export proof | `V.MSK0`, `V.MSK1` | any SFC/export/import edge lacks disposition or instance/harness owner | `COMPONENT-INVENTORY.json`, mount/export graph, consumer/deletion matrix |\n| `V.MSK3` state/API inventory | exact lifecycle/data/auth/network/a11y/motion applicability and fixtures; API/DI/store/worker/service-worker origins | `V.MSK1`, `V.MSK2` | generic shared state, undocumented `N/A`, unowned visible API error | `STATE-REGISTRY.json`, fixture catalog, API-visible-state matrix |\n| `V.MSK4` design formation | D1 brief and independent D2 critique for every page and each of 88 workflows | `V.MSK1`–`V.MSK3` | generic brief, removable decoration untested, no motion owner, missing exact copy | 14 route briefs, page-like-surface briefs, 88 workflow brief/critique rows, terminal dispositions |\n| `V.MSK5` Kronecker seal | generate applicable cells and machine-readable equivalence reductions; bind exact page/instance/harness owners | `V.MSK1`–`V.MSK4` | denominator changes without new version; orphan/duplicate/replayed witness; reduction lacks own-reason mutant | `KRONECKER-REGISTRY.json`, `EQUIVALENCE.json`, immutable denominator manifest and validator |\n| `V.MSK6` formation research loop | full-family Sol P1, true-Luna P2 bound to P1, fresh-Sol P3 bound to P2, two orthogonal hostile source reviews, owner agglomeration | `V.MSK5` | any family lacks all five dispositions; pass denominator/predecessor mismatch | sealed P1/P2/P3 registries, Review A/B, agglomeration receipt; still zero execution credit |\n| `V.MSK7` Apple/harness admission | authenticate installed Safari, iOS runtimes/devices, XCUITest/UI automation, deployed/local/API/offline origins, fixtures, capture tools and cleanup | `V.MSK6`; product coordinate expressly authorized later | emulation; unauthenticated localhost/deploy; shared database; missing teardown; coordinate mismatch | environment manifests, health receipts, no-write/cleanup proof, execution dispatch |\n| `V.MSK8` iOS Mobile Safari execution | execute every non-reduced cell on compact/large iPhone and applicable iPad; physical-device escalation | `V.MSK7` | missing raw packet; shared receipt; Simulator-only claim for unsupported behavior | raw per-cell packets and immutable iOS index |\n| `V.MSK9` desktop Safari execution | execute every non-reduced desktop cell with required windows/zoom/input/a11y/lifecycle/performance states | `V.MSK7` | WebKit substitute; missing installed Safari coordinate; missing raw packet | raw per-cell packets and immutable desktop index |\n| `V.MSK10` defect agglomeration | join iOS/desktop findings by source owner; write exact remediation specs, tests, tolerances, and rerun cells | `V.MSK8`, `V.MSK9` | defect closed by prose, screenshot, or unrelated platform | defect DAG, remediation wave specs, born-RED tests, owner routes |\n| `V.MSK11` authorized remediation and rerun | future product implementation only after separate authorization; rerun all affected/equivalent cells | `V.MSK10` and explicit execution authority | source change without born-RED or evidence; stale evidence; tolerance drift | product commits, tests, raw reruns, package/deploy receipts; outside this packet's authority |\n| `V.MSK12` convergence | seal evidence, independent Clean A, absorb findings, genuinely later Clean B, owner/root intake | `V.MSK11`; all denominator cells pass or retain explicit accepted RED | self-admission; same audit reused; any evidence or credit field not hash-bound | final manifest, Clean A/B, admission packet; no automatic release credit |\n\nWave file bounds are tranche artifacts under\n`docs/tranches/V/megatranche/audit/mobile-safari/**` until `V.MSK11` receives a\nseparate product authorization. Each wave owns disjoint artifact names and a\nsingle manifest. A future product wave must name exact source/test bounds and\nuse external isomorphic tests with module-child filename de-duplication.\n\n## 9. Typed DAG and negative edges\n\n```text\nlaw + product-coordinate + root-chronology\n  -> route/page inventory\n  -> component/export/mount inventory\n  -> state/API/fixture inventory\n  -> design briefs + critiques\n  -> Kronecker registry + equivalence proof\n  -> P1 -> P2 -> P3 -> hostile reviews -> agglomeration\n  -> real Apple/harness admission\n  -> iOS Safari raw cells + desktop Safari raw cells\n  -> defect DAG -> authorized remediation -> affected-cell rerun\n  -> evidence seal -> Clean A -> absorption -> genuinely later Clean B\n  -> owner/root admission\n```\n\nRequired negative edges:\n\n- Chromium, device emulation, the in-app Browser, Playwright WebKit, and image\n  rendering do not satisfy iOS or desktop Safari cells;\n- old 72/88 component and 218/264 axis evidence does not satisfy this new\n  platform matrix; the newer 88/88 and 264/264 values are specification only;\n- a router declaration or stub does not prove the mounted page;\n- a page receipt does not satisfy a child component and a harness receipt does\n  not satisfy a mounted instance;\n- a shared component receipt cannot satisfy different route, container, auth,\n  API, or data coordinates without a sealed equivalence proof;\n- an active sibling task, candidate, clean review, or dependency handoff does\n  not advance a Value cell;\n- no Value-to-Keyframes package edge, no raw parse-that source import, no\n  source alias, no copied Glass CSS, and no compatibility path is introduced;\n- parser selection/release/rebind remains PAUSED and cannot be inferred from\n  this audit;\n- Fourier storage selection remains independent; `LOCAL-SNAPSHOT` stays the\n  Value default and complex candidates remain unselected;\n- Glass development candidates do not satisfy the required final published\n  immutable Glass artifact;\n- product, API, package, release, or Browser mutation requires a new explicit\n  authorization and cannot be smuggled through a test-harness receipt.\n\n## 10. Performance and visual acceptance\n\nEach applicable cell must retain measurements in declared units and exact\ntools. At minimum:\n\n- navigation/interaction latency, long-task and main-thread occupancy,\n  layout/paint cost, memory growth, GPU/canvas behavior, scroll/drag frame\n  pacing, repeated open/close/reorder stability, background/resume, and BFCache;\n- geometry bounds, clipping, safe-area intrusion, keyboard occlusion, target\n  size, text truncation/wrap, popover/dialog containment, and scroll ownership;\n- semantic state and measured geometry/pixel DELTA within a versioned tolerance\n  manifest; never PNG byte equality;\n- motion frame samples at declared times, interruption/reversal behavior, and\n  immediate final seating under reduced motion where specified;\n- exact state copy, title/H1/landmark/name/role/value/live-region results,\n  focus movement, VoiceOver output, and contrast/text-scale findings.\n\nBudgets and tolerances remain RED until the responsible measurement tool,\nunits, baseline hardware, sample count, aggregation, threshold, and manifest\nlocus are sealed. A visually pleasant screenshot is not a performance receipt.\n\n## 11. Current counters and remaining gaps\n\n| Counter | Current value | Credit meaning |\n|---|---:|---|\n| governing Safari law bound | 1/1 | plan authority only |\n| named router paths source-joined | 14/14 | identity only; 0 Safari page executions |\n| wildcard rule source-joined | 1/1 | identity only; 0 redirect/error executions |\n| physical SFC paths/content source-joined | 88/88 | identity only; 0 Safari workflow executions |\n| existing D/L/C specification axes | 264/264 | specification only; 0 Apple-platform execution credit |\n| demo visual barrel declarations observed | 25/25 | declaration census only; mounted/harness disposition 0/25 sealed |\n| mount/source declaration edge floor | 115 observed | instance denominator remains OPEN |\n| page-like non-route surface denominator | OPEN | route/pane/mount join required |\n| mounted component-instance denominator | OPEN | predicates, duplicates, portals, and runtime conditions not sealed |\n| applicable Kronecker cell denominator | OPEN | cannot freeze before `V.MSK1`–`V.MSK5` |\n| subject-specific D1 route briefs under this law | 0/14 | RED |\n| component-specific D1/D2 rows under this law | 0/88 | RED |\n| real iOS Simulator Mobile Safari receipts | 0 | RED |\n| physical iOS escalation receipts | 0 | RED/conditional |\n| installed desktop Safari receipts | 0 | RED |\n| authenticated deployed-origin receipts | 0 | RED |\n| isolated real API/offline fixture receipts | 0 | RED |\n| new-law P1/P2/P3 formation passes | 0/3 | RED |\n| new-law hostile source reviews | 0/2 | RED |\n| final Clean A/Clean B | 0/2 | RED |\n| product/browser/visual/execution/API/package/release credit | 0 in every class | binding truth |\n\nThe immutable existing matrices remain unchanged:\n\n- non-parser formation specification: **11/11 = 100%**;\n- parser-law formation: **14/34 = 41.18%**, **PAUSED**;\n- Mobile Safari Kronecker execution: **0 executed cells**, with the denominator\n  intentionally not frozen until the source, state, mount, export, platform,\n  and equivalence registries close.\n\nIt would be a false positive to divide zero by the preliminary 14 routes, 88\nSFCs, 25 exports, or 115 declaration edges and call the result the final audit\npercentage. Those are overlapping source projections, not the Kronecker\ndenominator.\n\n## 12. Terminal dispositions\n\n| Concept | Disposition | Receiver |\n|---|---|---|\n| Mobile Safari Kronecker law | **KEEP** | `V.MSK0`–`V.MSK12` |\n| 14-route, 88-SFC, and 264-axis Value formation work | **KEEP** as inventory/specification input | `V.MSK1`–`V.MSK4` |\n| page, mounted-instance, and exported-unmounted harness ownership | **SPLIT** | `V.MSK1`, `V.MSK2` |\n| route-stub and out-of-band pane selection | **FOLD** into one authenticated route-to-render graph | `V.MSK1` |\n| debug and GenericActionBar deletion intent | **MOVE** to terminal source-deletion proof; current physical surfaces remain auditable | `V.MSK2` then future product owner |\n| old Chromium/Pixel-7 Browser findings | **KEEP** as negative archaeology; **PRUNE** from Safari credit | `V.MSK3`, `V.MSK10` |\n| emulation, WebKit, shared screenshots, shared component rows, unproved `N/A` | **PRUNE** | validator hostiles |\n| generic decorative Glass/card/gradient/motion choices | **PRUNE** unless measured-color or interaction evidence proves ownership | D2 critiques |\n| temporary disposable frontend/API/Docker harnesses | **KEEP** only with exact identity and cleanup receipt | `V.MSK7` |\n| parser work | **KEEP PAUSED** | external dependency boundary only |\n| product/API/package/release edits | **BLOCKED** | separate future authorization |\n\n## 13. Commit and handoff law\n\nThis source-only owner mark is one documentation artifact and should remain one\nformation-scoped commit if the parent later authorizes a commit. No product\nfile, package file, lockfile, generated distribution, Browser state, API data,\nor release coordinate belongs in that commit.\n\nFuture waves commit only after their born-RED gate, implementation/evidence,\nvalidator, and diff-check are complete. Broad gate/status and generated\nregistry commits require bodies naming the authority, exact evidence, credit\nvector, and routed remainder. Every wave hands the parent a compact receipt\ncontaining artifact paths/hashes, denominator version, pass/review identities,\nblocked dependencies, and zero-credit fields.\n\n## 14. Owner conclusion\n\nValue now has an exact source-only route for a full real-Safari audit. The\nsource seeds are reconciled at 14 named paths, one wildcard rule, 88 physical\nSFCs, 25 visual barrel declarations, and a 115-edge declaration floor. That is\nnot yet the audit denominator. The missing work is the route-to-render join,\npage-like and mounted-instance census, export/harness classification, exact\nstate/API/fixture inventory, 14 route and 88 component design briefs/critiques,\nKronecker applicability/equivalence seal, full Sol/Luna/Sol formation loop,\ntwo hostile reviews, authenticated real Apple environments, raw iOS and\ndesktop Safari execution, remediation, rerun, and two final clean audits.\n\nUntil those gates close, Value remains formation-specified but Apple-platform\nunexecuted: parser PAUSED, Safari evidence zero, and every product-facing credit\nzero.\n",
