      "encoding": "utf8",
      "content": "// The demo program (inv-K-1 — K.W2 split; N.W1.C mechanism-C resolution).\n//\n// `demo/` only. Resolves the value.js library through its PUBLISHED subpath\n// `exports` — `@mkbabb/value.js` + `@mkbabb/value.js/{color,parsing,math,easing,\n// units,transform,quantize}` → the `dist/*.d.ts` trust boundary (the T.W1\n// demo-dogfood keystone; the pre-keystone `@src/*` source path was RETIRED so\n// the demo speaks only the 8 public keys and no `src/` internal is reachable) —\n// and `@mkbabb/glass-ui` from its published `dist/` surface (N.W1.C / mechanism-C —\n// the `development` source-resolution condition was abrogated constellation-\n// wide; glass-ui's `exports` map carries only `{types, import, default}` → all\n// `dist/`). Dist-resolution gives a real `.d.ts` trust boundary: glass-ui's\n// declaration files are skip-checked (`skipLibCheck`, tsconfig.base.json), so\n// vue-tsc reports glass-ui's own internal diagnostics NEVER — the demo\n// typecheck sees ZERO foreign errors and needs no error-scoping filter. This is\n// why `npm run typecheck` is now the plain direct `vue-tsc -p` gate (the K.W2\n// `scripts/check-types.mjs` foreign-error filter was retired at N.W1.C; under\n// source-resolution it masked ~164 glass-ui-source diagnostics, which the dist\n// trust boundary now eliminates structurally).\n//\n// glass-ui's published `dist/` imports the value.js core by the bare\n// `@mkbabb/value.js` specifier (aurora/color paths, inv-K-2); a package never\n// installs itself, so the demo aliases that specifier to value.js's own\n// published `dist/value.js` (mirroring the Vite alias in `vite.config.ts`) for\n// one consistent published surface.\n//\n// This is the ONLY value.js program that may see glass-ui; the library program\n// (tsconfig.lib.json) never does (inv-K-1 — structurally glass-ui-free).\n{\n    \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.base.json\",\n    \"compilerOptions\": {\n        \"paths\": {\n            // W43 (RF-15): the demo `@…` path aliases were killed — every demo\n            // import is relative to its physical home. No `@styles`/`@components`/\n            // `@utils`/`@lib`/`@composables`/`@assets` project alias survives.\n            \"vue\": [\"./node_modules/vue\"],\n            \"@vue/*\": [\"./node_modules/@vue/*\"],\n            // The value.js published surface: the bare `.` root + the 7 subpath\n            // barrels, each → its `dist/*.d.ts` (the T.W1 demo-dogfood keystone;\n            // TS `paths` needs an explicit per-subpath entry — there is no `.../*`\n            // wildcard because the `exports` map is a CLOSED 8-key set). Mirrors\n            // the `vite.config.ts` runtime self-alias generated from the same map.\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js\": [\"./dist/index.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/color\": [\"./dist/subpaths/color.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/parsing\": [\"./dist/subpaths/parsing.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/math\": [\"./dist/subpaths/math.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/easing\": [\"./dist/subpaths/easing.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/units\": [\"./dist/subpaths/units.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/transform\": [\"./dist/subpaths/transform.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/quantize\": [\"./dist/subpaths/quantize.d.ts\"]\n        }\n    },\n    // `src/vite-env.d.ts` carries `/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />`\n    // (typing `import.meta.env`, `*.css`, `*?worker`) + the `*.vue`\n    // ambient module declaration. The pre-split unified program included it via\n    // `src/`; the demo graph needs it for the value.js `src/` modules it pulls in\n    // through `@src/*` and for its own Vite-specific imports.\n    \"include\": [\"demo/\", \"src/vite-env.d.ts\"]\n}\n",
      "live": {
        "absent": false,
        "bytes": 3665,
        "mode": "0644",
        "nlink": 1,
        "sha256": "10342b6fce51bd2a39f3f3b32512ec16f46149140d009f1404aea3c6aa6a83f5",
        "content": "// The demo program (inv-K-1 — K.W2 split; N.W1.C mechanism-C resolution).\n//\n// `demo/` only. Resolves the value.js library through its PUBLISHED subpath\n// `exports` — `@mkbabb/value.js` + `@mkbabb/value.js/{color,parsing,math,easing,\n// units,transform,quantize}` → the `dist/*.d.ts` trust boundary (the T.W1\n// demo-dogfood keystone; the pre-keystone `@src/*` source path was RETIRED so\n// the demo speaks only the 8 public keys and no `src/` internal is reachable) —\n// and `@mkbabb/glass-ui` from its published `dist/` surface (N.W1.C / mechanism-C —\n// the `development` source-resolution condition was abrogated constellation-\n// wide; glass-ui's `exports` map carries only `{types, import, default}` → all\n// `dist/`). Dist-resolution gives a real `.d.ts` trust boundary: glass-ui's\n// declaration files are skip-checked (`skipLibCheck`, tsconfig.base.json), so\n// vue-tsc reports glass-ui's own internal diagnostics NEVER — the demo\n// typecheck sees ZERO foreign errors and needs no error-scoping filter. This is\n// why `npm run typecheck` is now the plain direct `vue-tsc -p` gate (the K.W2\n// `scripts/check-types.mjs` foreign-error filter was retired at N.W1.C; under\n// source-resolution it masked ~164 glass-ui-source diagnostics, which the dist\n// trust boundary now eliminates structurally).\n//\n// glass-ui's published `dist/` imports the value.js core by the bare\n// `@mkbabb/value.js` specifier (aurora/color paths, inv-K-2); a package never\n// installs itself, so the demo aliases that specifier to value.js's own\n// published `dist/value.js` (mirroring the Vite alias in `vite.config.ts`) for\n// one consistent published surface.\n//\n// This is the ONLY value.js program that may see glass-ui; the library program\n// (tsconfig.lib.json) never does (inv-K-1 — structurally glass-ui-free).\n{\n    \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.base.json\",\n    \"compilerOptions\": {\n        \"paths\": {\n            // W43 (RF-15): the demo `@…` path aliases were killed — every demo\n            // import is relative to its physical home. No `@styles`/`@components`/\n            // `@utils`/`@lib`/`@composables`/`@assets` project alias survives.\n            \"vue\": [\"./node_modules/vue\"],\n            \"@vue/*\": [\"./node_modules/@vue/*\"],\n            // The value.js published surface: the bare `.` root + the 7 subpath\n            // barrels, each → its `dist/*.d.ts` (the T.W1 demo-dogfood keystone;\n            // TS `paths` needs an explicit per-subpath entry — there is no `.../*`\n            // wildcard because the `exports` map is a CLOSED 8-key set). Mirrors\n            // the `vite.config.ts` runtime self-alias generated from the same map.\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js\": [\"./dist/index.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/color\": [\"./dist/subpaths/color.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/parsing\": [\"./dist/subpaths/parsing.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/math\": [\"./dist/subpaths/math.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/easing\": [\"./dist/subpaths/easing.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/units\": [\"./dist/subpaths/units.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/transform\": [\"./dist/subpaths/transform.d.ts\"],\n            \"@mkbabb/value.js/quantize\": [\"./dist/subpaths/quantize.d.ts\"]\n        }\n    },\n    // `src/vite-env.d.ts` carries `/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />`\n    // (typing `import.meta.env`, `*.css`, `*?worker`) + the `*.vue`\n    // ambient module declaration. The pre-split unified program included it via\n    // `src/`; the demo graph needs it for the value.js `src/` modules it pulls in\n    // through `@src/*` and for its own Vite-specific imports.\n    \"include\": [\"demo/\", \"src/vite-env.d.ts\"]\n}\n"
      },
